window.EF_CRUX_DOC_PAGES=["Static GK · Chapter 1 · First in India\n\n                      FIRST IN INDIA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 1 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (naam-swap traps, chronology, similar-\nsounding firsts), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Top Constitutional Officials — President vs VP Swap Trap\n  ● President: Dr. Rajendra Prasad (1950–61) · Vice-President: Dr. S. Radhakrishnan (1952–62)\n  ● PM: Jawaharlal Nehru (1949–64) · Deputy PM/Home Min.: Sardar Patel (1947–50)\n  ● CJI: Justice H.J. Kania (1950–51) · CEC: Sukumar Sen (1950–58) — UN elections Sudan/Cambodia bhi supervise\n  kiye\n  ● Speaker Lok Sabha: G.V. Mavalankar · Lokpal: Pinaki Chandra Ghose (2019–22)\n  ● President World Bank (Indian-origin): Ajay Banga (2023–Present) — global body head hai, Indian govt official\n  NAHI\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"PVD\" order trick\n President→VP→Deputy-PM order yaad rakho: Prasad(President) pehle aaya, Radhakrishnan(VP) baad mein — dono\n naam swap hote hain exam mein, isliye bolo \"Prasad-Purab, Radhakrishnan-Rok\" (Prasad pehla number). Ajay Banga =\n \"Bahar wala Banga\" — World Bank ek international body hai, isko \"first Indian government official\" wale sawaal se mat\n jodo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n President→PM→Deputy PM order poocha jaata hai — Prasad aur Radhakrishnan ko swap mat karo. Ajay Banga World\n Bank ka President hai (global body), na ki koi Indian government post.\n\n\n\n2. Military & Viceroys — Bengal vs India Governor-General\n  ● Governor-General of Bengal: Warren Hastings (1773–85) — Charter Act 1833 se PEHLE ka designation\n  ● Governor-General of India: Lord William Bentinck (1833–35) — Charter Act 1833 ke BAAD ka naya designation\n  ● First Viceroy: Lord Canning (1858–62) · Last British GG/Viceroy: Lord Mountbatten (1947–48)\n  ● First aur Last Indian GG: C. Rajagopalachari — Rajaji (1948–50)\n  ● First C-in-C Independent India: K.M. Cariappa(1949) · First Field Marshal: Manekshaw(1973) · First CDS: Bipin\n  Rawat(2020)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"1833 se pehle Bengal, baad mein India\" trick\n Hastings=Bengal(1773, purana/chota title) → Bentinck=India(1833, naya/bada title) — Charter Act 1833 ne\n designation upgrade kiya, jaise chota post se bada post mila ho. Rajaji = \"Rajaji hi shuru, Rajaji hi ant\" — Indian GG list\n mein wahi first bhi hai aur last bhi (kyunki position khud hi 1950 mein khatam ho gayi Republic banne par).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Governor-General of Bengal (Hastings,1773) ≠ Governor-General of India (Bentinck,1833) — Charter Act 1833 ke\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 1 · First in India\n\n pehle-baad ke alag designations hain, mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n3. Men's Firsts — Bindra vs Chopra Olympic Gold Trap\n ● Individual Olympic Gold (any event): Abhinav Bindra — Beijing 2008\n ● Olympic Gold — Track & Field: Neeraj Chopra — Tokyo 2021\n ● C.D. Deshmukh — first Indian RBI Governor (1943–49) AND first Ramon Magsaysay (Public Service, 1959) — do\n alag records, ek hi vyakti\n ● Squadron Leader to space: Rakesh Sharma(1984) · Everest without oxygen: Sherpa Phu Dorji(1984)\n ● ODI double century: Sachin Tendulkar(2010) · Three ODI double centuries: Rohit Sharma\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Bindra=Individual-first, Chopra=Athletics-first\" trick\n Bindra(2008) = sabse PEHLA individual gold (koi bhi event) — number bhi chota/purana (2008). Chopra(2021) = sabse\n PEHLA Track & Field gold — number bada/naya (2021), aur specific sirf athletics ke liye. Yaad rakho: \"B for Bindra, B\n for Beginning (overall first)\" vs \"C for Chopra, C for Category-specific (sirf track)\". Deshmukh = \"Do-shमुख\" (do mukh/do\n roles) — RBI Governor AND Magsaysay dono ek hi banda, alag mat kar do.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Individual Olympic Gold (any event) = Bindra(2008). Olympic Gold Track & Field = Chopra(2021). Dono \"first gold\" hain\n par scope alag — swap mat karo.\n\n\n\n4. Women Officials & Other Fields — Kalpana Chawla Ka Trap\n ● First Woman President: Pratibha Patil(2007–12) · First Woman PM: Indira Gandhi(1966–77)\n ● First Woman Judge: Anna Chandy(1937) · First Woman SC Judge: Meera Sahib Fathima Beevi(1989–92)\n ● First Woman Governor: Sarojini Naidu, UP(1947–49) · First Woman CM: Sucheta Kriplani, UP(1963–67)\n ● First IAS Officer(woman): Anna Rajam Malhotra(1951) · First IPS Officer(woman): Kiran Bedi(1972)\n ● Indian-origin woman in Space: Kalpana Chawla(1997) — US citizen thi, NOT \"first Indian woman in space\"\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Origin ≠ Citizenship\" trick\n Kalpana Chawla = \"Indian-ORIGIN\" (janm India mein, par US citizen ban chuki thi jab space gayi) — isliye title hi\n carefully likha hai \"Indian-origin woman in space\", \"first Indian woman\" nahi. Sunita Williams bhi isi trap mein aati hai\n (wo bhi US citizen hai). Yaad rakho: \"Origin=Jaha paida hua, Citizenship=Jaha ka passport hai\" — Chawla ka origin\n India, citizenship USA.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Kalpana Chawla = first Indian-ORIGIN woman in space (US citizen thi) — NOT the first Indian woman in space overall.\n Sunita Williams ko bhi isi galti se cite kiya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 1 · First in India\n5. Women in Sports — Everest Chronology Trap\n ● First Olympics participation(woman): Nora Margaret Polley, Tennis, Paris(1924)\n ● First Everest climb(woman): Bachendri Pal(1984)\n ● First Everest TWICE(woman): Santosh Yadav(1992)\n ● First Disabled woman Everest: Arunima Sinha(2013) · Oldest(55) woman Everest: Jyoti Ratra(2024)\n ● Two Olympic medals(badminton): P.V. Sindhu(Rio2016+Tokyo2020) · Two medals single edition: Manu\n Bhaker(Paris2024)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Pal-Yadav-Sinha\" Everest chain\n Chronology order: Pal(1984, pehli baar) → Yadav(1992, dusri baar/twice) → Sinha(2013, disabled) — number\n sequence khud hi ghatna-order hai, bas seedha ratt lo: \"Pehle चढ़ी(Pal), फिर दोबारा(Yadav), फिर despite disability(Sinha)\".\n Sindhu = 2 ALAG Olympics mein 2 medal (Rio+Tokyo). Bhaker = EK hi Olympics(Paris) mein 2 medal — dono \"two\n medals\" hain par ek across-editions, doosra single-edition.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n P.V. Sindhu = 2 medals across TWO different Olympics (Rio 2016 + Tokyo 2020). Manu Bhaker = 2 medals in a SINGLE\n edition (Paris 2024). Dono \"two medal\" records hain par scope alag.\n\n\n\n6. Major Awards — Radhakrishnan vs Shastri Bharat Ratna Trap\n ● First Nobel(India): Rabindranath Tagore, Literature(1913) · First Bharat Ratna: Dr. S. Radhakrishnan(1954)\n ● First Posthumous Bharat Ratna: Lal Bahadur Shastri(1966) — Radhakrishnan NAHI\n ● First Foreign Bharat Ratna: Abdul Ghaffar Khan(1987) · First Param Vir Chakra: Major Somnath Sharma(1950)\n ● First Jnanpith: G. Shankar Kurup, Malayalam(1965) · First Hindi Jnanpith: Sumitranandan Pant(1968)\n ● First Ramon Magsaysay(overall): Acharya Vinoba Bhave(1958) · First Grammy: Pt. Ravi Shankar(1967)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Overall-first vs Posthumous-first\" trick\n Radhakrishnan(1954) = sabse PEHLA Bharat Ratna EVER (zinda the jab mila). Shastri(1966) = sabse PEHLA Bharat Ratna\n JO MARNE KE BAAD mila (posthumous). Yaad rakho: \"Radha-1st Overall, Shastri-1st Sadgati (mrityu ke baad)\" — dono\n \"first\" hain par ek qualifier ke saath. Bhave = \"Vinoba\" naam khud \"V for Very first\" jaisa — Magsaysay ka sabse pehla\n winner.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Lal Bahadur Shastri = first Bharat Ratna diya gaya POSTHUMOUSLY, NOT overall first (wo Radhakrishnan, 1954, hain).\n Ye classic trap hai — dono \"first\" claims alag qualifier ke saath sahi hain.\n\n\n\n7. Education, Cinema, Transport, Communication — Chronology Firsts\n ● First University: Nalanda(Bihar, 427 CE) · First Open University: BR Ambedkar OU, Hyderabad(1982)\n ● First Silent Film: Raja Harishchandra(1913) · First Talking Film: Alam Ara(1931) · First 3-D: My Dear\n Kuttichathan(1984)\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 1 · First in India\n ● First Passenger Train: Mumbai–Thane, 34km(1853) · First Metro: Kolkata Metro(1984)\n ● First Newspaper: Hickey's Bengal Gazette, English(1780)\n ● First Indian Linguistic Daily: Samachar Darpan, Bengali(1818) · First Hindi Newspaper: Udant Martand(1826)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"1780-1818-1826\" newspaper-language chain\n Language-order chronologically: English(1780,Hickey's) → Bengali(1818,Samachar Darpan) → Hindi(1826,Udant\n Martand) — numbers seedhe badhte jaate hain, bas order English-Bengali-Hindi yaad rakho \"E-B-H bolke\". Film chain:\n Silent(1913,B&W-no-sound) → Talking(1931,sound aaya) → Technicolour(1953, रंग aaya) → 3D(1984,depth aaya) —\n har decade mein ek naya feature add hota gaya, jaise ek movie hi upgrade ho rahi ho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Newspaper firsts ki language-chronology poochhi jaati hai: English(1780)→Bengali(1818)→Hindi(1826). In teeno\n saalon aur languages ko sequence se hi yaad rakho, order swap mat karo.\n\n\n\n8. Space, Defence & Miscellaneous — Aryabhatta Launch-Site Trap\n ● First Satellite: Aryabhatta(1975) — Soviet cosmodrome (Kapustin Yar) se launch hua, Indian soil se NAHI\n ● First Indigenously Built Satellite: INSAT-2A(1992) · First Lunar Mission: Chandrayaan-1(2008)\n ● First Underground Nuclear Test: Pokhran(18 May 1974) · First Indigenous Missile: Prithvi(1988)\n ● First Nuclear Reactor: Apsara(Aug 1956) · First Indigenous Nuclear Submarine: INS Arihant(2016)\n ● First National Park: Jim Corbett(1936) · First Stock Exchange: BSE(1875) · Project Tiger launched: Jim\n Corbett(1973)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Aryabhatta = Indian naam, Soviet zameen\" trick\n Aryabhatta satellite ka NAAM Indian scientist ke naam pe hai, par LAUNCH SITE Soviet Union tha (Kapustin Yar\n cosmodrome) — India ke paas tab apna launch capability nahi tha. Yaad rakho: \"Naam Bharat ka, Zameen Russia ki\" —\n is nuance ko alag se lock karo, warna \"Indian soil se launch\" wale sawaal mein galat answer ho jaayega.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Aryabhatta(1975) = India ka PEHLA satellite, lekin ye Soviet cosmodrome(Kapustin Yar) se launch hua tha, Indian soil se\n nahi — ye ek frequently tested nuance hai.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Officials: Prasad(Pres)-Radhakrishnan(VP) → GG: Hastings(Bengal)-Bentinck(India) → Firsts: Bindra(individual gold)-\n Chopra(athletics gold) → Chawla(Indian-origin space, not first Indian woman) → Everest: Pal-Yadav(twice)-\n Sinha(disabled) → Bharat Ratna: Radhakrishnan(overall 1st)-Shastri(1st posthumous) → Newspapers: English(1780)-\n Bengali(1818)-Hindi(1826) → Aryabhatta satellite(Indian naam, Soviet launch site)\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain                                                                Static GK · Chapter 1 · First in India\n\n\n\n\n 1) Bindra(2008)=first individual Olympic Gold (any event). Chopra(2021)=first Track & Field Gold. Alag scope, mix mat\n karo.\n 2) Kalpana Chawla = first Indian-ORIGIN woman in space (US citizen thi) — NOT first Indian woman in space overall.\n 3) Bharat Ratna: Radhakrishnan(1954)=overall first. Shastri(1966)=first POSTHUMOUS. Dono \"first\" hain, alag\n qualifier.\n\n\n                      Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.1 First in India\n\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 5","Static GK · Chapter 2 · Largest, Highest and Longest in India\n\nLARGEST, HIGHEST AND LONGEST IN INDIA — MEMORY TRICK\n                        SHEET\n                        Static GK · Chapter 2 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (similar-sounding categories jaise area-vs-\npopulation, height-vs-length, claimed-vs-administered), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Largest Water Bodies — Wular vs Chilika Trap\n  ● Freshwater Lake: Wular Lake (J&K) · Brackish Water Lake: Chilika Lake (Odisha)\n  ● Artificial Lake: Govind Ballabh Pant Sagar / Rihand Dam (UP)\n  ● Delta: Sundarbans Delta (West Bengal) · Natural Port: Mumbai (Maharashtra)\n  ● River Island: Majuli, Brahmaputra River (Assam) · River without a Delta: Narmada\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Wular=Fresh, Chilika=Brackish\" trick\n Wular = \"W for Water, saaf paani\" (freshwater, J&K ki thandi jheel). Chilika = \"Chil\" jaisa khaara/salty sound — Odisha\n ke samundar-kinare wali brackish (khaara) paani ki jheel. Yaad rakho: \"Wular pahaadon mein saaf, Chilika samundar ke\n paas khaara\" — geography se hi dono ka paani-type match ho jaata hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Wular Lake = largest FRESHWATER lake (J&K). Chilika Lake = largest BRACKISH water lake (Odisha). Inhe swap mat karo\n — yeh pairing almost har saal poochi jaati hai.\n\n\n\n2. Largest District — Area vs Population Trap\n  ● Largest District by Population: Thane (Maharashtra)\n  ● Largest District by Area: Kutch (Gujarat)\n  ● Largest Desert: Thar Desert (Rajasthan) · Largest River Island: Majuli (Assam)\n  ● Largest Delta: Sundarbans (West Bengal) · Largest Brackish Lake: Chilika (Odisha)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Thane=logo se bhara, Kutch=zameen se bada\" trick\n Thane = Mumbai ke paas, sheher-jaisa, isliye \"Th for Thane, Th for Thickly-populated\". Kutch = Rajasthan ke bagal mein\n bada registan-jaisa khula area, isliye \"K for Kutch, K for Khula/vast area\". Do alag states, do alag superlatives —\n Maharashtra=population wala bada, Gujarat=area wala bada.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Kutch = largest district by AREA (Gujarat). Thane = largest district by POPULATION (Maharashtra). Prelims-level\n questions mein yeh frequently swap kar diya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 2 · Largest, Highest and Longest in India\n3. Largest Structures — Kolkata Ka 4-Title Sweep\n ● Largest Mosque: Taj-ul-Masajid (Bhopal, MP) · Largest Dome: Gol Gumbaz (Bijapur, Karnataka)\n ● Largest Cave Temple: Kailasa Temple (Ellora, Maharashtra) · Largest Corridor: Rameswaram Temple Corridor\n (TN)\n ● Largest Zoo, Museum, Planetarium, aur Cantilever Bridge(Howrah) — CHAARO Kolkata mein\n ● Largest Single Screen Cinema: Raj Mandir (Jaipur) · Largest Cattle Fair: Sonepur (Bihar)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Kolkata ka Fantastic-4\" trick\n Kolkata akela 4 \"largest\" titles sweep karta hai: Zoo + Museum + Planetarium + Cantilever Bridge(Howrah). Yaad rakho\n ek group photo jaisa: \"Kolkata mein Zoo dekha, Museum ghooma, Planetarium mein taare dekhe, aur Howrah Bridge\n paar kiya\" — sab ek hi shehar ki trip mein ho gaya, isliye sab EK JAGAH yaad rehta hai.\n\n\n\n4. Highest in India — Kangchenjunga vs K2 Trap\n ● Highest Peak (India-administered): Kangchenjunga, 8,586m (Sikkim–Nepal border)\n ● Highest peak overall in India's claimed territory: K2/Godwin-Austen (8,611m) — Pakistan-occupied Kashmir\n mein\n ● Highest Airport: Leh Airport(Ladakh) · Highest Waterfall: Kunchikal Falls, 455m(Karnataka)\n ● Highest Dam: Tehri Dam, 260.5m(Uttarakhand) · Highest Lake: Tso Lhamo(Sikkim)\n ● Tallest Statue in World: Statue of Unity(Gujarat) · Tallest Minaret: Qutub Minar(Delhi)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"K2=claimed par PoK, Kangchenjunga=administered\" trick\n K2 = \"Kabza nahi hai\" (India claim karta hai par actual control Pakistan ke paas hai, PoK mein hai). Kangchenjunga =\n \"Kabza hai\" (India ke real control mein, Sikkim border par). Yaad rakho: \"K2=sirf Kaagaz pe (claimed),\n Kangchenjunga=Kabze mein (administered)\" — jab bhi \"actually administered by India\" wording ho, Kangchenjunga hi\n answer hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n K2(8,611m) India ke claimed territory mein highest hai lekin Pakistan-occupied Kashmir mein sthit hai. \"Highest peak\n actually ADMINISTERED by India\" → Kangchenjunga(8,586m), NOT K2 — bahut common trap hai.\n\n\n\n5. Longest Rivers — Ganga vs Godavari vs Yamuna\n ● Longest River overall: Ganga River, 2,525 km\n ● Longest River of South India: Godavari River, 1,465 km (nickname \"Dakshin Ganga\")\n ● Longest Tributary: Yamuna River, 1,376 km\n ● Longest Glacier: Siachen Glacier, ~76 km · State with Longest Coastline: Gujarat, 2,340 km\n ● Longest Canal: Indira Gandhi Canal, 650km(Rajasthan) · Longest Road: Grand Trunk Road\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Ganga-Godavari-Yamuna\" 3-scope trick\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 2 · Largest, Highest and Longest in India\n\n Teen alag \"longest river\" records, teen alag scope: Ganga = OVERALL sabse lambi (2,525km, poore India mein).\n Godavari = SOUTH INDIA mein sabse lambi (\"Dakshin Ganga\" naam mein hi \"Ganga jaisi south mein\" hint hai). Yamuna\n = sabse lambi TRIBUTARY (khud independent river nahi, kisi aur mein milti hai). Bolo: \"Overall-Ganga, South-Godavari,\n Tributary-Yamuna\" — teeno ko merge mat karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Ganga=overall longest river. Godavari=South India mein longest (\"Dakshin Ganga\"). Yamuna=longest tributary. Teen\n alag records hain — inhe merge mat karo.\n\n\n\n6. Longest Infrastructure — Tunnel & Bridge Category Traps\n ● Longest Railway Tunnel: T-50, J&K, 12.77 km\n ● Longest National Highway Tunnel: Dr. Syama Prasad Mookerjee Tunnel, J&K, 9.28 km\n ● Longest River Bridge: Bhupen Hazarika Setu (Assam–Arunachal Pradesh)\n ● Longest Sea Bridge: Atal Setu / Mumbai Trans Harbour Link (Mumbai)\n ● Longest Dam: Hirakud Dam(Odisha) — LENGTH ke hisaab se, height ke hisaab se Tehri sabse highest hai\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"T-50=Train, Mookerjee=Motor\" trick\n T-50 = \"T for Track\" (railway tunnel, 12.77km, sabse lamba). Mookerjee Tunnel = \"M for Motor-road\" (NH/road tunnel,\n 9.28km) — dono J&K mein hain isliye confuse hote hain, par ek train ke liye hai, doosra gaadi ke liye. Bridge trick:\n Bhupen Hazarika = \"River paar\" (river bridge), Atal Setu = \"Sea paar\" (Mumbai ka samundar), Hirakud = \"Dam ki\n lambai\" (Tehri se confuse mat karo, wo height mein highest hai, Hirakud length mein longest hai).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n T-50(railway tunnel,12.77km) aksar Dr. Syama Prasad Mookerjee Tunnel(road/NH tunnel,9.28km) se confuse ho jaata\n hai — dono alag categories, dono J&K region mein hain. Aur Hirakud=longest dam(length), Tehri=highest dam(height)\n — alag superlatives.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Lakes: Wular(fresh)-Chilika(brackish) → District: Thane(population)-Kutch(area) → Kolkata sweep: Zoo-Museum-\n Planetarium-Howrah Bridge → Peak: Kangchenjunga(administered)-K2(claimed,PoK) → Rivers: Ganga(overall)-\n Godavari(South)-Yamuna(tributary) → Tunnels: T-50(rail)-Mookerjee(road) → Bridges: Bhupen Hazarika(river)-Atal\n Setu(sea) → Dam: Hirakud(length)-Tehri(height)\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Wular Lake=largest FRESHWATER lake. Chilika Lake=largest BRACKISH water lake. Har saal poochi jaati hai, swap\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 2 · Largest, Highest and Longest in India\n\nmat karo.\n2) Kutch=largest district by AREA(Gujarat). Thane=largest district by POPULATION(Maharashtra).\n3) \"Highest peak actually ADMINISTERED by India\" → Kangchenjunga(8,586m), NOT K2(8,611m, jo PoK mein hai par\nIndia claim karta hai).\n\n\n            Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.2 Largest, Highest and Longest in India\n\n\n\n\n                                            Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 3 · First in the World\n\n                FIRST IN THE WORLD — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                        Static GK · Chapter 3 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (closely-related milestones jaise space-vs-\nmoon, world-vs-country firsts, ek hi country ke do alag firsts), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Men's Firsts — Airship vs Airplane Timeline Trap\n  ● To fly an Airship: Henri Giffard (France, 1852)\n  ● To fly an Airplane (powered fixed-wing): Wright Brothers (America, 1903)\n  ● Theory of expansion of universe: Edwin Hubble (America, 1929)\n  ● First Black player to win Wimbledon: Arthur Ashe (America, 1975)\n  ● First Asian President of ICC: Jagmohan Dalmiya (India, 1997–2000)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Giffard-Gubbara, Wright-Windowless\" 51-saal-gap trick\n Giffard(1852) = Airship — socho ek gubbara(balloon-jaisa gas-filled craft) udaya, engine-controlled hi sahi par\n pankh(wings) nahi the. Wright Brothers(1903) = poora 51 saal BAAD aaye asli \"powered fixed-wing airplane\" leke.\n Yaad rakho: \"G for Gas-bag pehle (Giffard), W for Wings baad mein (Wright)\" — airship ne aadhi sadi pehle hi apni\n jagah bana li thi powered flight se.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Wright Brothers(1903, powered AIRPLANE) Henri Giffard(1852, AIRSHIP) ke 51 saal BAAD aaye — airship aur airplane\n do alag \"first flight\" milestones hain, inhe ek mat samjho.\n\n\n\n2. First in Space — Gagarin vs Armstrong Trap\n  ● First person to go into Space: Yuri Gagarin (Soviet Union, 1961)\n  ● First person to touch Moon's surface: Neil Armstrong (USA, 1969)\n  ● Youngest person in Space: Gherman Titov (Soviet Union, 1961) · First to walk in Space: Alexei Leonov (Soviet\n  Union, 1965)\n  ● First Space Tourist: Dennis Tito (USA, 2001) · Oldest astronaut in Space: John Glenn (77 years old)\n  ● First Space Tourist to travel TWICE: Charles Simonyi (USA, 2007 & 2009)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Gagarin=Space, Armstrong=Moon\" 8-saal-gap trick\n Gagarin(1961) = sirf SPACE mein pahuncha (orbit kiya, Moon nahi gaya). Armstrong(1969) = MOON ki surface pe pair\n rakha — poore 8 saal baad, ek alag achievement. Yaad rakho: \"Gagarin ne Gagan(sky/space) chua, Armstrong ne Moon\n chua\" — dono \"first man\" hain par alag destination, ek hi fact mat bana do.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Yuri Gagarin(1961) = SPACE mein jaane waale first. Neil Armstrong(1969) = MOON par jaane waale first. Do alag\n milestones, jinhe aksar ek hi \"first man in space\" fact maan liya jaata hai.\n\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 3 · First in the World\n3. Poles & Everest — Peary/Amundsen aur Everest Firsts\n ● First to reach North Pole: Robert Peary (USA, 1909)\n ● First to reach South Pole: Roald Amundsen (Norway, 1911) — baad mein North Pole bhi(1926), isliye DONO\n poles ka first\n ● First to climb Everest: Tenzing Norgay(Nepal) & Edmund Hillary(New Zealand), 1953\n ● Oldest man to climb Everest: Yuichiro Miura(Japan, 2013) · Climbing without Oxygen: Messner & Habeler(1978)\n ● First Voyage around the World: Ferdinand Magellan(1519–21)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Peary-North-Pehla, Amundsen-South-phir-North\" trick\n Peary(1909) = SIRF North Pole ka first (South kabhi nahi gaya). Amundsen(1911) = South Pole ka first, aur 1926 mein\n North bhi kar liya — isliye Amundsen hi wo akela vyakti hai jo DONO poles pe pehla pahuncha. Yaad rakho: \"P for\n Peary, P for Pehla-North-only\" vs \"A for Amundsen, A for All-two-poles\".\n\n\n\n4. Women's Firsts — Bandaranaike vs Indira Gandhi World-vs-Country Trap\n ● First Woman President in World: Maria Estela Perón (Argentina)\n ● First Woman PM in World: Sirimavo Bandaranaike (Sri Lanka)\n ● First Woman PM of UK: Margaret Thatcher(1979–90) · First Woman PM of Muslim country: Benazir\n Bhutto(Pakistan)\n ● First Woman in Space: Valentina Tereshkova(Soviet Union, 1963) · First Woman to walk in Space: Svetlana\n Savitskaya(1984)\n ● First Woman to climb Everest: Junko Tabei(Japan, 1975) · First woman to cross English Channel: Gertrude\n Ederle(USA, 1926)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Bandaranaike=World, Indira=Sirf India\" trick\n Bandaranaike(Sri Lanka) = DUNIYA ki first woman PM overall — chota desh, par WORLD record. Indira Gandhi = sirf\n INDIA ki first woman PM — bada desh, par sirf COUNTRY-level record. Yaad rakho: \"Bandaranaike=Bade Vishwa ki,\n Indira=India ki\" — jab bhi \"world first\" wording ho, Bandaranaike hi sahi answer hai, Indira Gandhi nahi.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Sirimavo Bandaranaike = duniya ki first woman PM (Sri Lanka). Indira Gandhi = sirf INDIA ki first woman PM. \"World\n first\" wale questions mein in dono ko mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n5. First Country — Political & Social Firsts\n ● First to organise Modern Olympics: Greece(1896) · First to win FIFA World Cup: Uruguay(1930)\n ● First to implement RTI: Sweden(1766) · First to appoint Lokpal/Ombudsman: Sweden(1809) — DO ALAG \"firsts\"\n ● First to grant women right to vote: New Zealand(1893) · First to abolish death penalty: Venezuela(1863)\n ● First written Constitution: USA(1789) · First to recognise same-sex marriage: Netherlands(2001)\n ● First to recognise euthanasia: Netherlands(2002) · First civil nuclear deal with India: France(2008)\n\n\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 3 · First in the World\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Sweden Double\" trick\n Sweden do baar aata hai is chapter mein, alag centuries mein: RTI(1766, purana) aur Ombudsman/Lokpal(1809, thoda\n baad). Yaad rakho: \"Sweden ne pehle SOOCHNA ka adhikaar diya(RTI,1766), phir SHIKAYAT sunne wala\n banaya(Ombudsman,1809)\" — dono Sweden ke hain par alag institutions, ek hi answer mein merge mat karo.\n Netherlands bhi do baar hai: same-sex marriage(2001) pehle, euthanasia(2002) baad mein.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Sweden do baar aata hai: first RTI law(1766) AND first Ombudsman/Lokpal-type office(1809) — yeh do alag \"firsts\"\n hain, aksar ek hi galat answer mein merge kar diye jaate hain.\n\n\n\n6. First Country — Science, Trade & World Institutions\n ● First to invent paper: China, Cai Lun(105 CE) · First to launch satellite into space: Russia — Sputnik(1957)\n ● First University (world's first): Takshashila University — ancient India mein thi, present-day Pakistan mein sthit\n ● First Nuclear Power Plant: Obninsk, Russia(1954) · First Cloned animal: Dolly the Sheep, Scotland(1996)\n ● First city destroyed by atomic bomb: Hiroshima, Japan(1945) · First international film festival: Venice(Italy,1932)\n ● First Cricket Club: Marylebone Cricket Club/MCC, England(1787) · First to issue plastic currency: Australia(1988)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Takshashila = Ancient-India, Modern-Pakistan\" trick\n Takshashila University = duniya ki first university mani jaati hai, par ye jis region mein thi (Punjab-belt) wo AB present-\n day Pakistan mein aata hai — \"jab bani thi India(undivided) mein thi, ab naksha badal gaya\". Yaad rakho: \"Takshashila\n = purani jagah India, aaj ki jagah Pakistan\" — geography-shift ka classic trap hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Takshashila University ko duniya ki first university mana jaata hai — yeh ancient India mein sthit thi (undivided), ek\n aise region mein jo present-day Pakistan mein aata hai.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Flight: Giffard(airship,1852)-Wright(airplane,1903) → Space: Gagarin(space,1961)-Armstrong(moon,1969) → Poles:\n Peary(North only)-Amundsen(both) → Everest: Tenzing-Hillary(1953) → Women PM: Bandaranaike(World)-\n Indira(India only) → Sweden double: RTI(1766)-Ombudsman(1809) → Takshashila(ancient India, modern Pakistan) →\n Sputnik(Russia,1957)-Obninsk(Russia,1954)\"\n\n\n                           Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Yuri Gagarin(1961)=first in SPACE. Neil Armstrong(1969)=first on MOON. Alag milestones, ek fact mat bana do.\n 2) Sirimavo Bandaranaike(Sri Lanka)=first woman PM in WORLD. Indira Gandhi=first woman PM of INDIA only. Mix\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 3 · First in the World\n\nmat karo.\n3) Sweden = first RTI(1766) AND first Ombudsman/Lokpal(1809) — do alag \"firsts\", ek answer mein merge mat karo.\n\n\n                  Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.3 First in the World\n\n\n\n\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 4 · Largest, Tallest and Smallest in the World\n\nLARGEST, TALLEST AND SMALLEST IN THE WORLD — MEMORY\n                      TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 4 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (naam-misleading cheezein jaise Caspian\n\"Sea\", country-vs-continent scale, elevation-vs-relief numbers), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag\nmein.\n\n1. Largest Geography — Caspian Sea Ka Naam-Trap\n  ● Largest Lake (saltwater): Caspian Sea (Russia) — naam mein \"Sea\" hai par yeh actually ek LAKE hai\n  ● Largest Freshwater Lake: Lake Superior (USA)\n  ● Largest Continent: Asia(44.58 million sq.km) · Largest Country by area: Russia(17.1 million sq.km)\n  ● Largest Ocean: Pacific Ocean · Largest Sea: South China Sea · Largest Island: Greenland(Denmark)\n  ● Largest Archipelago: Indonesia(13,500+ islands) · Largest Strait: Strait of Malacca\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Naam mein Sea, Asal mein Lake\" trick\n Caspian Sea = duniya ki sabse badi LAKE hai — par isme itna namkeen paani hai aur itna bada hai ki naam \"Sea\" pad\n gaya, exam isi confusion ko test karta hai. Yaad rakho: \"Caspian = Sea ka naam, Lake ka kaam\" (saltwater lake). Lake\n Superior = asli/pure FRESHWATER lake mein sabse badi. Dono \"largest lake\" hain par ek saltwater, ek freshwater —\n category miss mat karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Caspian Sea = duniya ki largest LAKE hai (saltwater lake, true sea nahi). Lake Superior = largest FRESHWATER lake hai.\n \"Sea\" naam hone ki wajah se Caspian commonly confuse hota hai.\n\n\n\n2. Largest Deserts — Antarctica vs Sahara vs Atacama\n  ● Largest Desert overall (by area): Antarctica Polar Desert — sabse bada, COLDEST desert\n  ● Largest HOT Desert: Sahara (Africa)\n  ● Driest Desert: Atacama Desert (Chile)\n  ● Largest River Island: Majuli(Assam,India) — is chapter mein World record ke saath overlap\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Antarctica-Bada, Sahara-Garam, Atacama-Sookha\" trick\n Teen alag desert-superlatives, teen alag qualities: Antarctica = OVERALL sabse bada (par thanda/cold hai — log\n \"desert\" sun ke garam sochte hain, yahi trap hai). Sahara = sabse bada GARAM/hot desert. Atacama = sabse\n SOOKHA/dry desert (baarish sabse kam). Bolo: \"Bada-Antarctica, Garam-Sahara, Sookha-Atacama\" — teeno ko ek mat\n samjho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Antarctica=overall largest desert(cold). Sahara=largest HOT desert. Atacama=DRIEST desert. Teen alag records hain jo\n aksar ek hi samajh kar test kiye jaate hain — inhe alag rakho.\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 4 · Largest, Tallest and Smallest in the World\n\n\n\n\n3. Largest Structures & Nature — India Ka Multi-Sweep\n ● Largest Stadium: Narendra Modi Stadium(Ahmedabad, India) · Largest Statue: Statue of Unity(India, 182m)\n ● Largest Solar Power Park: Bhadla Solar Park(Rajasthan, India — 2,245 MW)\n ● Largest Port: Shanghai(China) · Largest Airport: King Fahd Intl.(Dammam, Saudi Arabia)\n ● Largest Railway Station: Grand Central Terminal(New York, USA) · Largest Temple: Angkor Wat(Cambodia)\n ● Largest Animal: Blue Whale(~30m, ~100 tonnes) · Largest Bird: Ostrich\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"India ka triple-sweep\" trick\n India teen \"world's largest\" titles le raha hai: Stadium(Modi Stadium) + Statue(Statue of Unity) + Solar Park(Bhadla) —\n teeno modern/recent achievements hain, isliye ek group mein yaad rakho: \"India ne Stadium banaya, Statue khada\n kiya, aur Solar Park bhi bana diya\" — sab India ke naam. Baaki sab (Port-China, Airport-Saudi, Station-USA, Temple-\n Cambodia) alag-alag desh mein hai, ek-ek karke match karo.\n\n\n\n4. World's Longest — Hubli Platform Ka Double-Record\n ● Longest River: Nile River (11 African countries se guzarti hai)\n ● Longest Railway Platform: Hubli Railway Platform, 1,507m(Karnataka, India) — WORLD's AUR India's dono\n ● Longest Mountain Range: Andes(South America) · Longest Wall: Great Wall of China\n ● Longest Tunnel: Gotthard Base Tunnel(Switzerland) · Longest Railway Route: Trans-Siberian Railway(Russia)\n ● Longest Epic: Mahabharata\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Hubli = Do Medal Ek Sath\" trick\n Hubli Railway Platform ek hi cheez se DO records jeeta — India ka longest platform bhi, aur duniya ka longest platform\n bhi (kyunki India ka record hi world record ban gaya). Yaad rakho: \"Hubli = Do Trophy Ek Sath\" — jab bhi \"world's\n longest platform\" ya \"India's longest platform\" poocha jaaye, answer same hi hai — Hubli.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Hubli Railway Platform(India) ek saath World's longest AUR India's longest railway platform, dono records hold karta\n hai — same answer dono scopes ke liye kaam karta hai, koi alag world-record city nahi hai.\n\n\n\n5. World's Highest — Ojos del Salado Elevation Trap\n ● Highest Mountain Peak: Mount Everest(Nepal, 8,849m) · Highest Building: Burj Khalifa(Dubai, ~828m)\n ● Highest Active Volcano: Ojos del Salado(Argentina–Chile border, ~6,893m)\n ● Highest Motorable Pass: Umling La Pass(Ladakh, India — ~5,083m)\n ● Highest Waterfall: Angel Falls(Venezuela, ~979m) · Highest Navigable Lake: Lake Titicaca(South America,\n 3,812m)\n ● Highest Dam: Jinping-I Dam(China, ~305m) · Highest Plateau: Tibetan Plateau(~4,500m avg)\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 4 · Largest, Tallest and Smallest in the World\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"6,893 not 3,500\" number-lock trick\n Ojos del Salado ki PEAK ELEVATION ~6,893m hai — kabhi-kabhi notes mein galti se \"average height\" 3,500m likh diya\n jaata hai (base-to-summit relief ka number hai, elevation nahi). Yaad rakho: \"Ojos ki asli height =Everest se sirf thodi\n kam (8,849 vs 6,893) — chota number(3,500) galat hai, bada number(6,893) sahi hai\". Ye duniya ka highest ACTIVE\n volcano hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Ojos del Salado ki peak elevation approx 6,893m hai (kabhi-kabhi galat tarike se \"average height\" 3,500m likha jaata\n hai) — yeh duniya ka highest active volcano hai. Elevation ko base-to-summit relief ke saath confuse mat karo.\n\n\n\n6. World's Smallest — Vatican vs Australia Scale Trap\n ● Smallest Country: Vatican City(Europe, 0.49 sq.km)\n ● Smallest Continent: Australia(~3 million sq.km)\n ● Smallest River: Roe River(Montana, USA, ~61 metres) · Smallest Bird: Bee Hummingbird(Cuba, ~5.5cm, ~1.6g)\n ● Countries with shortest border: Spain and Morocco(85m)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Vatican=Desh, Australia=Mahadeep\" scale trick\n Vatican City = sabse chota COUNTRY hai (0.49 sq.km, ek park jaisa chota). Australia = sabse chota CONTINENT hai (~3\n million sq.km — phir bhi Vatican se LAKHON guna bada, kyunki scale hi alag hai — desh vs mahadeep). Yaad rakho:\n \"Vatican=Chota Ghar, Australia=Chota Mahal\" — dono \"smallest\" hain par tulna ka scale bilkul alag hai, kabhi mix mat\n karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Vatican City = smallest COUNTRY. Australia = smallest CONTINENT. Yeh do alag scales hain — \"smallest landmass\" wale\n questions mein inhe mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Caspian Sea(largest lake, saltwater)-Superior(largest freshwater) → Deserts: Antarctica(bada,cold)-Sahara(hot)-\n Atacama(dry) → India triple-sweep: Modi Stadium-Statue of Unity-Bhadla Solar Park → Hubli Platform(world+India\n dono) → Ojos del Salado(6,893m elevation, not 3,500m relief) → Vatican(smallest country)-Australia(smallest\n continent)\"\n\n\n                           Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Caspian Sea = largest LAKE(saltwater, not a true sea). Lake Superior = largest FRESHWATER lake. Naam se confuse\n mat ho.\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 4 · Largest, Tallest and Smallest in the World\n\n2) Antarctica=largest desert overall(cold). Sahara=largest HOT desert. Atacama=DRIEST desert. Teen alag records.\n3) Vatican City=smallest COUNTRY. Australia=smallest CONTINENT. Alag scale hai, mix mat karo.\n\n\n        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.4 Largest, Tallest and Smallest in the World\n\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 5 · Places Related to Prominent People\n\n  PLACES RELATED TO PROMINENT PEOPLE — MEMORY TRICK\n                        SHEET\n                        Static GK · Chapter 5 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (ek hi vyakti ki multiple places — birth vs\ndeath vs achievement — jo aapas mein confuse ho jaati hain), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag\nmein.\n\n1. Gautam Buddha — 4 Life Events Ki Sequence\n  ● Lumbini(Nepal) → Birth\n  ● Bodhgaya(Bihar) → Enlightenment\n  ● Sarnath(UP) → First Sermon (Dharmachakra Pravartana)\n  ● Kushinagar(UP) → Mahaparinirvana (Death)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"LBSK\" life-stage chain\n Sequence order mein yaad karo: Lumbini(janm) → Bodhgaya(gyaan) → Sarnath(pehla updesh) → Kushinagar(mrityu) =\n \"L-B-S-K\". Bolo: \"Life Begins, Spreads, Koncludes\" — janm se maut tak ek seedhi yatra, teen alag states (Nepal, Bihar,\n UP-UP) mein hoti hai. Bodhgaya aur Sarnath dono ek hi region(Bihar-UP border) ke paas hain isliye inhe order se hi\n yaad rakho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Buddha ke 4 life-stages order mein baar-baar poochhe jaate hain:\n Lumbini(birth)→Bodhgaya(enlightenment)→Sarnath(1st sermon)→Kushinagar(death). Sequence swap mat karo.\n\n\n\n2. Mahavira & Guru Nanak — Bihar Ke 2 Confusable Sites\n  ● Mahavira — Birth: Kundagram(Bihar)\n  ● Mahavira — Nirvana/Death: Pawapuri(Bihar)\n  ● Guru Nanak — Birth: Talwandi, ab Nankana Sahib(Pakistan)\n  ● Buddha ka enlightenment(Bodhgaya) bhi Bihar mein hai — teen jagah ek hi state mein\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Kunda-Birth, Pawa-Paar\" trick\n Kundagram = \"Kunwara\" (bachpan/janm) — Mahavira ka janm-sthal. Pawapuri = \"Paar/Pooran\" (jeevan ka ant/paar\n lagna) — Mahavira ka nirvana-sthal. Dono Bihar mein hain isliye confuse hote hain — yaad rakho\n \"Kunda=Kunwara=Shuru, Pawa=Paar=Ant\". Guru Nanak ka birth-place ab Pakistan mein hai (Nankana Sahib) — naam\n badal gaya, desh bhi badal gaya (Partition ke baad).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Buddha ka enlightenment(Bodhgaya) aur Mahavira ka birth(Kundagram)+death(Pawapuri) — teeno Bihar mein hain,\n mix up karna aasaan hai ki kaunsa event kis jagah se juda hai.\n\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 5 · Places Related to Prominent People\n3. Spiritual & Social Reformers — Ashram-Person Match\n ● Aurobindo Ghosh → Puducherry (Ashram established)\n ● Rabindranath Tagore → Santiniketan, West Bengal (Visva-Bharati founded; UNESCO World Heritage Site 2023)\n ● Ramakrishna Paramahamsa → Belur Math, West Bengal (1897 — Ramakrishna Mission HQ)\n ● Vinoba Bhave → Paunar, Maharashtra (Brahma Vidya Mandir Ashram)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"2 Bengal, 2 Alag\" trick\n Do reformers West Bengal mein hain — Tagore(Santiniketan) aur Ramakrishna(Belur Math) — dono alag jagah, dono\n alag kaam: Tagore ne UNIVERSITY(Visva-Bharati) banayi, Ramakrishna Mission ne HQ(Belur Math) banaya. Yaad rakho:\n \"Tagore=Padhai(university), Ramakrishna=Mission(HQ)\". Santiniketan 2023 mein UNESCO Heritage bana — ye RECENT\n fact hai, current-affairs-linked question mein alag se poochha ja sakta hai.\n\n\n\n4. Gandhi & Nehru — Teen Murti vs Anand Bhavan Trap\n ● Gandhi — Birth: Porbandar(Gujarat) · Sabarmati Ashram: Dandi March launch(1930)\n ● Gandhi — Sevagram Ashram(Maharashtra, 1936–48)\n ● Nehru — Teen Murti Bhavan(New Delhi): Official PM Residence\n ● Nehru — Anand Bhavan(Allahabad): Ancestral/family home\n ● Sardar Patel: Bardoli Satyagraha(Gujarat, 1928) · Rajendra Prasad: Birth — Jiradei, Siwan(Bihar)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Teen Murti=Kaam, Anand Bhavan=Ghar\" trick\n Teen Murti Bhavan = \"Teen\" (matlab yahan Nehru ne PM ke roop mein kaam kiya, official/work residence) — New\n Delhi mein. Anand Bhavan = \"Anand\" (khushi/family, purana ghar) — Allahabad mein, Nehru ka bachpan ka ancestral\n ghar. Yaad rakho: \"Teen Murti=Trabajo(kaam ki jagah), Anand Bhavan=Aashiyana(ghar)\" — dono Nehru se judi hain\n par role bilkul alag.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Teen Murti Bhavan = Nehru ki official PM residence(New Delhi). Anand Bhavan = unka ancestral family\n home(Allahabad). Dono Nehru se linked hain lekin alag roles serve karte hain — commonly swap ho jaate hain.\n\n\n\n5. Foreign Personalities — Birth vs Death Place Traps\n ● Jesus Christ: Jerusalem(Israel) — Death and Resurrection\n ● Prophet Muhammad: Mecca(Saudi Arabia) — Birth\n ● Alexander the Great — Birth: Macedonia(Greece) · Death: Babylon(Iraq)\n ● Napoleon — Birth: Corsica(France) · Defeated: Waterloo(Belgium, 1815)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Birth-desh-alag, Death-desh-alag\" trick\n Do foreign leaders ka birth aur \"end\" alag-alag desh mein hua — Alexander: Macedonia(Greece) mein paida,\n Babylon(Iraq) mein mara — East ki taraf jeetta-jeetta wahin dam toda. Napoleon: Corsica(France) mein paida,\n\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 5 · Places Related to Prominent People\n\n Waterloo(Belgium) mein haara — apne hi Europe mein ghoom kar downfall hua. Yaad rakho: \"Dono ke liye Birth-\n country ≠ End-country\" — is pattern ko dono logon pe apply karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Napoleon Corsica(French island) mein paida hue the lekin famously Waterloo, Belgium(1815) mein DEFEAT hue —\n birth aur downfall do alag countries mein. Alexander bhi isi pattern mein hai: Macedonia(birth) vs Babylon(death).\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Buddha: L-B-S-K(Lumbini-Bodhgaya-Sarnath-Kushinagar) → Mahavira: Kundagram(birth)-Pawapuri(death), dono\n Bihar → Guru Nanak: Talwandi/Nankana Sahib(Pakistan) → Reformers: Tagore(Santiniketan,university)-\n Ramakrishna(Belur Math,mission) → Gandhi: Porbandar(birth)-Sabarmati(Dandi March)-Sevagram(ashram) → Nehru:\n Teen Murti(kaam)-Anand Bhavan(ghar) → Alexander: Macedonia(birth)-Babylon(death) → Napoleon: Corsica(birth)-\n Waterloo(defeat)\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Buddha's 4 life-stages sequence: Lumbini(birth)→Bodhgaya(enlightenment)→Sarnath(1st\n sermon)→Kushinagar(death) — order kabhi swap mat karo.\n 2) Teen Murti Bhavan = Nehru ki PM office-residence(Delhi). Anand Bhavan = unka ancestral family ghar(Allahabad)\n — alag roles hain.\n 3) Napoleon: Corsica(birth, France) vs Waterloo(defeat, Belgium) — birth-country aur downfall-country alag hain.\n\n\n            Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.5 Places Related to Prominent People\n\n\n\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 6 · Popular Nicknames of Famous Personalities\n\n         POPULAR NICKNAMES OF FAMOUS PERSONALITIES —\n                     MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                        Static GK · Chapter 6 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (ek vyakti ke multiple titles, ya do alag\nlogon ka same title), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Literary & Historical Titles — Chanakya Ka Triple-Naam\n  ● Shakespeare of India: Mahakavi Kalidasa\n  ● Napoleon of India: Samudra Gupta\n  ● India's Machiavelli: Chanakya — Kautilya bhi kehte hain, Arthashastra ke author bhi\n  ● Vidyasagar (Ocean of Knowledge): Ishwar Chandra Bandyopadhyay\n  ● Mahamana (Great Soul): Pt. Madan Mohan Malaviya — BHU ke founder\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Chanakya=Kautilya=Machiavelli=Arthashastra-writer\" trick\n Chanakya ke 3 naam/titles EK hi vyakti ko refer karte hain: Chanakya(asli naam) = Kautilya(dusra naam) = India's\n Machiavelli(title, political-cunning ke liye) = Arthashastra ka author. Yaad rakho: \"4 naam, 1 aadmi\" — jaise bhi option\n mein aaye, sab same answer hain. Kalidasa=Shakespeare(dono poet-playwright), Samudra Gupta=Napoleon(dono\n military-genius) — comparison ka LOGIC bhi yaad rakho, ratt nahi.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Chanakya ke titles exams mein pile ho jaate hain: \"India's Machiavelli\", \"Kautilya\", aur \"Arthashastra ke author\" — sab\n EK hi vyakti ko refer karte hain, aksar alag options banakar test kiya jaata hai ki aap jaante ho ki yeh ek hi vyakti hai.\n\n\n\n2. Freedom Fighters — Ek-Nazar Mein Sabke Titles\n  ● Father of the Nation/Bapu/Mahatma: Mahatma Gandhi · Chacha Nehru/Panditji: Jawaharlal Nehru\n  ● Lokmanya: Bal Gangadhar Tilak · Iron Man of India/Sardar: Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel\n  ● Netaji: Subhas Chandra Bose · Babasaheb: B.R. Ambedkar · Gurudev: Rabindranath Tagore\n  ● Shaheed-e-Azam: Bhagat Singh · Man of Peace: Lal Bahadur Shastri\n  ● Frontier Gandhi/Badshah Khan: Khan Abdul Ghaffar Khan — Khudai Khidmatgar movement lead kiya\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Frontier Gandhi ≠ Gandhi\" trick\n Frontier Gandhi(Khan Abdul Ghaffar Khan) ka naam mein \"Gandhi\" hai isliye confuse hota hai — par yeh Mahatma\n Gandhi se BILKUL ALAG vyakti hain, North-West Frontier(Pakistan-belt) ke leader the, Khudai Khidmatgar movement\n chalaya. Yaad rakho: \"Frontier=Seema-par ka Gandhi jaisa\" — similarity sirf non-violence ki soch mein hai, naam-\n conflict mat karo. Baaki titles seedhe match hain: Bapu=Gandhi, Netaji=Bose, Babasaheb=Ambedkar — inhe apna\n signature-word samajh ke ratt lo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 6 · Popular Nicknames of Famous Personalities\n\n Khan Abdul Ghaffar Khan = \"Frontier Gandhi\" (North-West Frontier region) — inhone Khudai Khidmatgar movement\n lead kiya. Inhe Mahatma Gandhi ke saath confuse mat karo — naam mein \"Gandhi\" hai par alag vyakti hain.\n\n\n\n3. Regional Leaders — \"Deenbandhu\" Shared-Title Trap\n ● Andhra Kesari: T. Prakasam(Andhra Pradesh)\n ● Lion of Bengal/Deenbandhu: C.F. Andrews(Bengal — \"Friend of the Poor\")\n ● Lion of Bihar/Bihar Kesari/Deenbandhu: Dr. Shrikrishna Singh(Bihar)\n ● Jan Nayak(People's Leader): Karpoori Thakur — 49th Bharat Ratna recipient\n ● Sher-e-Kashmir: Sheikh Abdullah · Punjab's Tagore: Puran Singh · Babuji: Jagjivan Ram\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Deenbandhu Do Logon Ka\" trick\n \"Deenbandhu\" title DO alag logon ko diya gaya hai — C.F. Andrews(Bengal ke Lion) AND Dr. Shrikrishna Singh(Bihar ke\n Lion). Yaad rakho: \"Deenbandhu = Do-bandhu\" (do logon ka common title) — jab bhi \"Deenbandhu\" akela poocha\n jaaye, sawaal mein REGION(Bengal ya Bihar) dhyan se dekho, tabhi sahi vyakti pata chalega. \"Lion of X\" pattern bhi is\n title ke saath judta hai dono jagah.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n \"Deenbandhu\" title do alag logon ke beech shared hai — C.F. Andrews(Lion of Bengal) aur Dr. Shrikrishna Singh(Lion of\n Bihar). Same title, alag personalities — paired region-title ko dhyan se check karo.\n\n\n\n4. Sports & Arts Icons — Nightingale Ka Do-Field Trap\n ● Wizard of Hockey: Dhyan Chand · The Flying Sikh: Milkha Singh\n ● Haryana Hurricane: Kapil Dev · Flicker Singh: Sandeep Singh — drag-flick specialist hockey captain\n ● The Nightingale of India/Bharat Kokila: Sarojini Naidu — poet aur freedom fighter\n ● The Nightingale of Melody: Lata Mangeshkar — playback singer\n ● Mother Teresa: Nirmal Hriday (home for the dying) se associated\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Nightingale-India=Kavita, Nightingale-Melody=Gaana\" trick\n Dono \"Nightingale\" hain par bilkul alag field: Naidu = Nightingale of INDIA(desh ke liye poem/freedom-struggle mein\n awaaz uthayi). Mangeshkar = Nightingale of MELODY(sur/gaane ki awaaz). Yaad rakho: \"India=Desh-bhakti(Naidu),\n Melody=Sangeet(Lata)\" — dono \"bulbul jaisi meethi awaaz\" ke liye jaani jaati hain par kaam alag (poet-politician vs\n singer).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n \"Nightingale of India\" (Sarojini Naidu, poet-freedom fighter) vs \"Nightingale of Melody\" (Lata Mangeshkar, playback\n singer) — similar titles, bilkul alag fields.\n\n\n\n\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath                              Static GK · Chapter 6 · Popular Nicknames of Famous Personalities\n\n\n\n\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Chanakya=Kautilya=Machiavelli=Arthashastra-writer(1 vyakti,4naam) → Frontier Gandhi(Ghaffar Khan) ≠ Mahatma\n Gandhi → Deenbandhu: C.F.Andrews(Bengal)-Shrikrishna Singh(Bihar), do alag log → Nightingale: Naidu(India,poet)-\n Lata(Melody,singer) → Sabke titles: Bapu-Gandhi, Netaji-Bose, Babasaheb-Ambedkar, Gurudev-Tagore, Lokmanya-\n Tilak\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Chanakya = Kautilya = India's Machiavelli = Arthashastra ka author — sab EK hi vyakti, exam alag options bana ke\n confuse karta hai.\n 2) Frontier Gandhi(Khan Abdul Ghaffar Khan) — naam mein \"Gandhi\" hai par Mahatma Gandhi se BILKUL ALAG vyakti\n hain.\n 3) \"Deenbandhu\" title do logon ka hai: C.F. Andrews(Lion of Bengal) aur Dr. Shrikrishna Singh(Lion of Bihar) — region\n check karke hi answer do.\n\n\n        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.6 Popular Nicknames of Famous Personalities\n\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 7 · Facts Related to Major Countries of the World\n\n    FACTS RELATED TO MAJOR COUNTRIES — MEMORY TRICK\n                         SHEET\n                        Static GK · Chapter 7 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (country-specific naming conventions,\nhistorical-vs-modern agencies, naam-credit traps), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Parliaments — Bicameral Names Ka Country-Match\n  ● India: Lok Sabha + Rajya Sabha · USA: Congress — Senate + House of Representatives\n  ● Russia: Duma(Lower) + Federation Council(Upper) · China: National People's Congress\n  ● Japan: Diet · Germany: Bundestag · Israel: Knesset · Sweden: Riksdag · Taiwan: Yuan\n  ● Britain/Ireland/S.Africa/Malaysia/Canada/France: simply \"Parliament\"\n  ● Bangladesh: Jatiya Sansad · Iran/Maldives: Majlis · Afghanistan: Shura/National Assembly\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"1 country, 1 unique naam\" hook\n Har bade desh ka parliament-naam uska OWN identity hai — koi do bade desh same naam share nahi karte(sirf\n \"Parliament\" generic use karne wale kai desh hain, unhe alag group mein rakho). Chota mnemonic: \"Diet khaate Japan\n mein, Duma bolte Russia mein, Knesset Israel ka gहना\" — sound-based hook se yaad karo. Bicameral upper-lower\n naam ek favourite one-mark question hai, isliye India/USA/Russia teeno ka dono-house naam pakka karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Bicameral naam yaad rakho: India(Lok Sabha+Rajya Sabha), USA(Senate+House), Russia(Duma+Federation Council). Ek\n house naam per country ek favourite one-mark question hai — teeno desh mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n2. Intelligence Agencies — KGB Ka Historical-vs-Modern Trap\n  ● India: RAW, CBI, IB · Pakistan: ISI · America: CIA, NSA, FBI · Britain: MI5, MI6, GCHQ\n  ● Israel: Mossad · Russia: GRU; KGB(purani, Soviet-era) · Germany: BND · France: DGSE\n  ● China: MSS + International Liaison Department · Japan: Naicho · Canada: CSIS\n  ● Iran: VAJA/MOIS\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"KGB=Purana, GRU=Naya\" trick\n KGB = SOVIET-ERA ki agency thi, ab formally EXIST nahi karti (Soviet Union khatam ho gaya 1991 mein). Modern Russia\n ki agency = GRU(military intelligence)/SVR. Yaad rakho: \"KGB = Kal ki baat(purana), GRU = Guzarte waqt ki naveen\n agency\" — exam agar \"CURRENT Russian agency\" poochhe toh GRU/SVR bolo, \"historical Soviet agency\" poochhe toh\n KGB bolo. Context dhyan se padho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n KGB Soviet-era ki agency thi; modern Russia ki external intelligence GRU/SVR hai. KGB ab formally exist nahi karti lekin\n historically list ki jaati hai — exam context check karo answer dene se pehle.\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 7 · Facts Related to Major Countries of the World\n3. Documents & Reports — Colour-Code Se Country-Group\n ● Blue Book: Britain · White Book: Germany, China, Portugal · Green Book: Italy, Iran\n ● Orange Book: Netherlands · Grey Book: Japan, Belgium · Yellow Book: France(Livre Jaune)\n ● Beige Book: USA · White Paper: India(specific subject), Britain, China\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Colour se, country se nahi\" trick\n Country ke bajaye COLOUR se group karke yaad rakho — fast recall ke liye. \"Blue=Britain(1 desh),\n White=Germany/China/Portugal(3 desh), Yellow=France, Beige=USA\" — colour hi memory-key hai. Yaad rakho:\n \"White\" sabse zyada crowded rang hai(3 countries)+White Paper bhi alag se hai — inhe ek dusre se mat jodo, White\n Book aur White Paper do alag documents hain.\n\n\n\n4. Official Residences — India Ke President-vs-PM\n ● President of India: Rashtrapati Bhavan(New Delhi) · PM of India: 7, Lok Kalyan Marg(New Delhi)\n ● President of USA: White House · President of Russia: Kremlin · President of France: Élysée Palace\n ● PM of Britain: 10, Downing Street · The Monarch(Britain): Buckingham Palace\n ● President of China: Zhongnanhai · PM of Nepal: Singha Durbar/Baluwatar\n ● President of Pakistan: Aiwan-e-Sadr · President of Bangladesh: Bangabhavan\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Rashtrapati Bhavan=President, Lok Kalyan Marg=PM\" trick\n India mein DO alag residences hain — Rashtrapati Bhavan(sirf PRESIDENT ke liye) aur 7,Lok Kalyan Marg(PM ke liye).\n Yaad rakho: \"Rashtrapati=Bhavan(bada mahal, ceremonial head), PM=Marg(rasta/address, executive head)\" — dono\n naam ki feel bhi role match karti hai (Bhavan=grand, Marg=working address). Britain mein bhi do alag hain:\n Buckingham Palace(Monarch/Raja-Rani) vs 10 Downing Street(PM).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n India ke President Rashtrapati Bhavan mein rehte hain, lekin PM ki official residence 7, Lok Kalyan Marg\n hai(Rashtrapati Bhavan nahi) — beginners aksar isse mix up karte hain.\n\n\n\n5. Landmarks — Statue of Liberty, Eiffel Tower Key Facts\n ● Statue of Liberty(New York) — France ka gift, Bartholdi ne design kiya, unveiled 28 Oct 1886\n ● Eiffel Tower(Paris) — Gustave Eiffel ne banaya(1887–89), Height 1,083 feet\n ● Mount Rushmore(South Dakota) — Washington, Jefferson, T.Roosevelt, Lincoln ke faces\n ● Elba(Italy) — Napoleon ke exile ka jagah(1814) · Red Square(Moscow) — Lenin's Mausoleum\n ● Davos(Switzerland) — World Economic Forum(WEF) annual meetings host karta hai\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"France ne diya, France ne banaya\" trick\n Statue of Liberty = France ka GIFT tha America ko (Bartholdi ne design kiya, French sculptor). Eiffel Tower = France ke\n apne shehar(Paris) mein Gustave Eiffel ne banaya. Yaad rakho: \"France double role — kisi ko gift diya(Liberty), khud ke\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 7 · Facts Related to Major Countries of the World\n\n liye bhi banaya(Eiffel)\" — dono French designers/builders hain, isliye France ka naam do jagah aata hai, confuse mat\n ho ki dono same location pe hain.\n\n\n\n6. Landmarks — Angkor Wat Ka Hindu-se-Buddhist Transition\n ● Angkor Wat(Cambodia) — Largest religious monument, UNESCO site — ORIGINALLY Hindu(Vishnu) temple,\n baad mein Buddhist ban gaya\n ● Grand Canal(China) — world's longest man-made canal · Temple of Heaven(Beijing) — 1406–1420 AD\n ● Al-Aqsa Mosque(Jerusalem) — third holiest mosque after Mecca aur Medina\n ● Opera House(Sydney) — world-famous cultural centre · Amsterdam — diamond cutting industry\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Angkor Wat = Hindu se Buddhist safar\" trick\n Angkor Wat pehle VISHNU(Hindu) ko dedicated tha, samay ke saath BUDDHIST site ban gaya — ek hi mandir ne apna\n dharm badla. Yaad rakho: \"Angkor Wat = Vishnu se shuru, Buddha tak pahuncha\" — is transition ko chapter 7's\n Wonders section mein bhi cross-check karo (wahan bhi yeh trap repeat hota hai, \"8th Wonder\" wale context mein).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Angkor Wat ek HINDU temple ke roop mein shuru hua tha(Vishnu ko dedicated) aur baad mein Buddhist site mein\n convert ho gaya — yeh ek frequently tested transition hai.\n\n\n\n7. Seven Wonders — Angkor Wat \"8th Wonder\" Trap\n ● New 7 Wonders: Great Wall of China, Petra(Jordan), Machu Picchu(Peru), Christ the Redeemer(Brazil), Roman\n Colosseum(Italy), Chichén Itzá(Mexico), Taj Mahal(India)\n ● Taj Mahal — 1632 AD, Shah Jahan ne Mumtaz Mahal ke liye banaya\n ● Machu Picchu — 1430 AD, Hiram Bingham ne 1911 mein discover kiya, 2,450m Inca site\n ● Great Wall of China — 7th century BC, Length 21,196 km\n ● Angkor Wat = popularly \"8th Wonder\" kaha jaata hai LEKIN official list ka PART NAHI hai\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Angkor Wat 8th hai, 7 mein nahi\" trick\n Angkor Wat ko log \"8th Wonder\" bolte hain(informal nickname) — par ye OFFICIAL New 7 Wonders list mein SHAAMIL\n NAHI hai. Yaad rakho: \"8th = Extra, Official-7 mein nahi\" — jab bhi \"New 7 Wonders list mein kaunsa hai\" poochha\n jaaye, Angkor Wat ko mat chuno, wo bonus/8th hai list ke BAHAR. King Suryavarman II ne banwaya tha, originally\n Hindu temple.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Angkor Wat ko aksar \"8th Wonder\" kaha jaata hai lekin yeh official New Seven Wonders list ka part NAHI hai — ek\n favourite trick question. King Suryavarman II dwara banaya gaya, originally ek Hindu temple tha.\n\n\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 7 · Facts Related to Major Countries of the World\n8. World Travellers — Vespucci Ka Naam-Credit Trap\n ● Amerigo Vespucci(Italy) — America unke naam par hai, discovered S.America coast(1501) aur Amazon\n mouth(1499)\n ● Christopher Columbus(Spain-sponsored) — Discovery of America, Cuba, West Indies(1492)\n ● Vasco da Gama(Portugal) — first European to reach India by sea(1498)\n ● Roald Amundsen(Norway) — South Pole(1911) AND North Pole(1926)\n ● Sir Francis Drake(Britain) — circumnavigated world in single voyage(1577–80)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"America=Vespucci ka naam, Columbus ne pehle dhoonda\" trick\n Columbus(1492) ne America \"discover\" kiya — par continent ka NAAM Amerigo Vespucci(baad mein aaya, 1501) ke\n naam par pada, kyunki Vespucci ne samjha ki ye ek \"New World\" hai(naya continent), na ki Asia ka hissa jaisa\n Columbus sochta tha. Yaad rakho: \"Columbus=Pehla Pair rakha, Vespucci=Sahi Pehchaan ki\" — isi wajah se naming-\n credit Vespucci ko mila, Columbus ko nahi.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Amerigo Vespucci Italian the lekin unki voyages Spain/Portugal dwara sponsored thi — America unke naam par hai,\n Columbus ke naam par NAHI, halaanki Columbus \"discovering America\" se zyada commonly juda hai.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Parliaments: India(LS+RS)-USA(Congress)-Russia(Duma+FedCouncil)-Japan(Diet) → KGB(purani,Soviet)-\n GRU(naya,modern) → Documents: colour-se-group(Blue-Britain,Yellow-France) → Residences: Rashtrapati\n Bhavan(President)-Lok Kalyan Marg(PM) → Statue of Liberty+Eiffel(dono France-linked) → Angkor\n Wat(Hindu→Buddhist, 8th Wonder-not-official) → Vespucci(naming credit)-Columbus(first landed)\"\n\n\n                            Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) KGB=Soviet-era(purani), modern Russia ki agency=GRU/SVR. KGB ab formally exist nahi karti.\n 2) India: President=Rashtrapati Bhavan, PM=7 Lok Kalyan Marg — dono alag residences, mix mat karo.\n 3) Angkor Wat ko \"8th Wonder\" kaha jaata hai par official New 7 Wonders list ka PART NAHI hai.\n\n\n        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.7 Facts Related to Major Countries of the World\n\n\n\n\n                                            Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 8 · Capitals, Currencies and Languages\n\n  CAPITALS, CURRENCIES AND LANGUAGES — MEMORY TRICK\n                         SHEET\n                        Static GK · Chapter 8 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (shared currency naam, split countries,\nfamous-city-vs-capital traps), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Asia — \"Rupee\" 5 Countries Mein Shared Trap\n  ● India: New Delhi, Rupee, Hindi/English · Pakistan: Islamabad, Rupee, Urdu/Sindhi/Punjabi\n  ● Nepal: Kathmandu, Nepalese Rupee, Nepali · Sri Lanka: Colombo, Rupee, Sinhalese/Tamil\n  ● Mauritius: Port Louis, Rupee, English/French/Bhojpuri/Hindi\n  ● Japan: Tokyo, Yen · China: Beijing, Yuan(Renminbi) · South Korea: Seoul, Won\n  ● Myanmar: Naypyidaw, Kyat · Afghanistan: Kabul, Afghani · Bhutan: Thimphu, Ngultrum\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"5 desh, 1 currency-naam\" trick\n \"Rupee\" naam 5 ALAG countries mein use hota hai — India, Pakistan, Nepal(Nepalese Rupee), Sri Lanka, Mauritius.\n Yaad rakho: \"IPNSM\" (India-Pakistan-Nepal-SriLanka-Mauritius) — jab bhi sawaal mein sirf \"Rupee\" likha ho, DESH ka\n naam dhyan se padho, default-assume mat karo ki Indian Rupee hi hai. South Asia ka pura neighborhood(+Mauritius)\n is currency-family mein hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Kai Asian countries currency naam ke roop mein \"Rupee\" use karte hain — India, Pakistan, Nepal(Nepalese Rupee), Sri\n Lanka, Mauritius. Mixed-country question mein \"Rupee\" ko hamesha Indian Rupee mat samajh lena.\n\n\n\n2. Europe — Euro-Users vs Non-Euro Exceptions\n  ● Euro use karte hain: Germany, France, Italy, Netherlands, Belgium, Spain\n  ● Euro NAHI use karte: UK(Sterling Pound), Russia(Ruble), Norway(Krone), Denmark(Danish Krone),\n  Ukraine(Hryvnia), Belarus(Ruble)\n  ● Germany: Berlin, German · France: Paris, French · Italy: Rome, Italian\n  ● UK: London, English · Russia: Moscow, Russian\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"6 Euro-club, 6 Bahar\" trick\n Europe do groups mein baant do: EURO-CLUB(Germany, France, Italy, Netherlands, Belgium, Spain — mostly\n Western/Central) vs NON-EURO(UK, Russia, Norway, Denmark, Ukraine, Belarus — mostly \"apni currency pe proud\"\n desh). Yaad rakho: \"6 desh Euro mein mile, 6 desh apni currency pe ade rahe\" — UK ne jaan-boojhkar Euro nahi\n liya(Sterling se emotional attachment), Norway-Denmark bhi apni Krone rakhte hain.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Zyada tar Western European countries Euro use karte hain(Germany, France, Italy, Netherlands, Belgium, Spain). UK,\n Russia, Norway, Denmark, Ukraine, Belarus Euro NAHI use karte — exceptions yaad rakho.\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 8 · Capitals, Currencies and Languages\n\n\n\n\n3. Africa — Sudan vs South Sudan Split Trap\n ● Sudan: Khartoum(capital), Sudanese Pound, Arabic\n ● South Sudan: Juba(capital), South Sudanese Pound, English — 2011 mein Sudan se SPLIT hua\n ● Morocco: Rabat, Moroccan Dirham, Arabic/Berber · Nigeria: Abuja, Naira, English\n ● Egypt: Cairo, Egyptian Pound, Arabic · Algeria: Algiers, Algerian Dinar, Arabic/Berber\n ● Libya: Tripoli, Libyan Dinar, Arabic\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Sudan-Khartoum-Arabic, South Sudan-Juba-English\" trick\n Sudan aur South Sudan 2011 mein SPLIT hue — do alag desh, do alag capital, aur ek unique fact: Sudan Arabic bolta\n hai, par South Sudan(naya desh) ENGLISH ko official language banaya(Arabic se door jaane ke liye). Yaad rakho:\n \"Sudan=Purana-Khartoum-Arabic, South Sudan=Naya-Juba-English\" — naya desh ne jaan-boojhkar alag language\n choose ki apni pehchaan banane ke liye.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Sudan aur South Sudan do alag countries hain(2011 mein split hue) with different capitals — Khartoum(Sudan) vs\n Juba(South Sudan). Frequently ek hi nation samajh liya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n4. Americas — Brazil Ka Odd-One-Out Language\n ● North America: USA(Washington DC,Dollar), Canada(Ottawa,Canadian Dollar,Eng/French), Mexico(Mexico\n City,Peso,Spanish)\n ● South America mostly SPANISH: Argentina, Chile, Venezuela, Colombia, Peru\n ● Brazil = ODD ONE OUT — Brasília(capital), Real(currency), PORTUGUESE(not Spanish)\n ● Venezuela currency: Bolívar(naam se \"peso\" nahi) · Peru currency: Sol\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Brazil=Portugal ka Beta\" trick\n South America mein LAGBHAG har desh SPANISH bolta hai — Argentina, Chile, Venezuela, Colombia, Peru — par\n BRAZIL akela PORTUGUESE bolta hai. Yaad rakho: \"Brazil = Portugal ka colony tha, baaki sab Spain ke colony the\" — isi\n history se language-pattern samjho. Bolo: \"South America mein Brazil hi Portuguese-wala island hai\" — sabse bada\n desh(area/population) hone ke bawajood akela alag bhasha.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Brazil South America mein odd one out hai — iski official language Portuguese hai, jabki lagbhag har doosra South\n American country Spanish bolta hai.\n\n\n\n5. Australia/Oceania — Canberra vs Sydney Capital Trap\n ● Australia: CANBERRA (capital) — Sydney NAHI, English, Australian Dollar\n ● New Zealand: Wellington(capital), New Zealand Dollar, English/Māori\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 8 · Capitals, Currencies and Languages\n\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Canberra=Capital, Sydney=Famous\" trick\n Sydney = Australia ka sabse BADA/mashhoor sheher hai(Opera House, harbour) — par capital NAHI hai. Canberra =\n actual capital, chota planned city hai jo specially isi purpose ke liye banaya gaya (jaise India mein New Delhi vs\n Mumbai). Yaad rakho: \"Sydney=Star(famous), Canberra=Sarkar(capital)\" — jitni fame Sydney ki hai, capital ka title phir\n bhi Canberra ke paas hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Canberra, Sydney nahi, Australia ki capital hai — Sydney sirf largest aur sabse well-known city hai, yeh GK exams mein\n ek bahut common trap hai.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Asia: Rupee-club(India-Pakistan-Nepal-SriLanka-Mauritius) → Europe: Euro-6(Germany-France-Italy-Netherlands-\n Belgium-Spain) vs Non-Euro-6(UK-Russia-Norway-Denmark-Ukraine-Belarus) → Africa: Sudan(Khartoum,Arabic)-South\n Sudan(Juba,English) → Americas: Brazil(Portuguese, odd-one-out) → Oceania: Canberra(capital)-Sydney(famous but\n not capital)\"\n\n\n                           Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) \"Rupee\" 5 alag countries mein hai: India, Pakistan, Nepal, Sri Lanka, Mauritius — desh ka naam dhyan se padho.\n 2) Sudan(Khartoum,Arabic) aur South Sudan(Juba,English) 2011 mein split hue — do alag desh, ek nation mat samjho.\n 3) Canberra, Sydney NAHI, Australia ki capital hai — Sydney sirf largest/famous city hai.\n\n\n            Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.8 Capitals, Currencies and Languages\n\n\n\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 9 · Authors and Their Books\n\n       AUTHORS AND THEIR BOOKS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 9 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (ek author ki multiple books, similar-\nsounding naam wale alag log, biography-vs-autobiography), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Ancient & Classical Authors — Kalidasa Ke Big-3\n  ● Kalidasa: Abhijnana Shakuntalam(drama), Raghuvansham(epic), Meghasandesam(lyric poem) — \"Big 3\"\n  ● Kautilya: Arthashastra · Panini: Ashtadhyayi · Bharatamuni: Natya Shastra · Charak: Charaka Samhita\n  ● Banabhatta: Harshacharita, Kadambari · Kalhana: Rajatarangini · Jayadeva: Geet Govindam\n  ● Ashvaghosha: Buddhacharita · Megasthenes: Indica · Vishakhadatta: Mudrarakshasa\n  ● Harshavardhana(raja, khud author): Priyadarshika, Nagananda, Ratnavali\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Kalidasa ka 3-genre Big-3\" trick\n Kalidasa ki sabse zyada books hain(7), par 3 SABSE IMPORTANT alag-alag GENRE cover karti hain: Abhijnana\n Shakuntalam(DRAMA/natak) → Raghuvansham(EPIC/mahakavya) → Meghasandesam(LYRIC/geet-kavya). Yaad rakho:\n \"Natak-Mahakavya-Geet\" teen alag style, ek hi author — jab bhi Kalidasa ka naam confuse ho, ye teeno pehle pakka\n karo, baaki 4 baad mein.\n\n\n\n2. National Leaders — Vande Mataram Anandamath Ke Andar\n  ● Bankim Chandra Chatterjee: Anandamath(novel) — \"Vande Mataram\" ISI ke ANDAR embedded hai, alag book\n  NAHI\n  ● Nehru: Discovery of India, Glimpses of World History · Gandhi: Hind Swaraj, My Experiments with Truth\n  ● Ambedkar: The Annihilation of Caste, Waiting for a Visa, The Buddha and His Dhamma\n  ● Rajendra Prasad: India Divided, Satyagraha in Champaran · Azad: India Wins Freedom\n  ● Modi: Exam Warriors, Jyotipunj · Draupadi Murmu: Wings to Our Hopes · Kejriwal: Swaraj\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Vande Mataram = Anandamath ka hissa\" trick\n \"Vande Mataram\" koi ALAG standalone book nahi hai — ye Bankim Chandra ke novel \"Anandamath\" ke ANDAR ek\n geet/song hai. Yaad rakho: \"Anandamath = Ghar, Vande Mataram = Us ghar ka ek kamra\" — poori book alag hai, ek\n chapter/song usi ke andar hai. Exam mein \"Vande Mataram kis book ka part hai\" poochha jaaye toh answer\n Anandamath, na ki koi separate title.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n \"Vande Mataram\" Bankim Chandra Chatterjee ke novel \"Anandamath\" ke andar embedded hai — yeh ek separate\n standalone book NAHI hai, exams mein ek common misconception.\n\n\n\n3. Modern Indian Authors — Tharoor Ki Do-Naam Ek-Book\n  ● Shashi Tharoor: same book, do titles — \"An Era of Darkness\"(UK market) / \"Inglorious Empire\"(India market)\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 9 · Authors and Their Books\n ● Tharoor: The Great Indian Novel, Ambedkar: A Life, Why I am a Hindu\n ● Arundhati Roy: The God of Small Things, Azadi: Freedom, Fascism, Fiction\n ● Chetan Bhagat: Half Girlfriend, Two States · Sarojini Naidu: Golden Threshold, Broken Wing\n ● Anita Desai: In Custody\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Ek Book, Do Bazaar, Do Naam\" trick\n Shashi Tharoor ki ek hi book ke DO alag titles hain — India mein \"An Era of Darkness\" naam se chhapi, UK mein\n \"Inglorious Empire\" naam se. Yaad rakho: \"Darkness=India ka naam, Inglorious=UK ka naam\" — content same\n hai(British Raj ki criticism), sirf market ke hisaab se publisher ne title badla. Exam kisi bhi ek naam se poochh sakta hai,\n dono yaad rakho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Shashi Tharoor ki ek book ke do markets ke liye do titles hain: \"An Era of Darkness\"(India) aur \"Inglorious Empire\"(UK)\n — same book, region ke hisaab se alag title.\n\n\n\n4. Sports Books — Player-Title Quick Match\n ● Abhinav Bindra: A Shot at History · Kapil Dev: Straight from the Heart · Sunil Gavaskar: Sunny Days\n ● Milkha Singh: The Race of My Life · Mary Kom: Unbreakable · Sachin Tendulkar: Playing it My Way\n ● Saina Nehwal: Playing to Win · Sania Mirza: Ace Against Odds · Sourav Ganguly: A Century is Not Enough\n ● Yuvraj Singh: The Test of My Life · VVS Laxman: 281 and Beyond · P.T. Usha: Golden Girl\n ● Syed Kirmani: Stumped · Ravi Shastri: Stargazing\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Title=Career-signature\" trick\n Har sports-book ka title unke career ki ek SIGNATURE moment/theme se juda hai — VVS Laxman(\"281 and Beyond\") =\n unki famous 281-run innings se naam liya. Sania Mirza(\"Ace Against Odds\") = tennis term \"Ace\" + unka struggle-story.\n Ganguly(\"A Century is Not Enough\") = ek century se santusht na hone wala attitude. Yaad rakho: \"Title padho, career-\n highlight yaad aa jaayega, wahi se author confirm ho jaayega\".\n\n\n\n5. International Authors — Aristophanes vs Aristotle Naam-Trap\n ● Aristophanes(playwright): Lysistrata, Plutus, The Clouds — Aristotle(philosopher) SE ALAG vyakti hai\n ● Karl Marx: Das Kapital, The Communist Manifesto · George Orwell: Animal Farm, 1984\n ● Shakespeare: Hamlet, Macbeth, Romeo and Juliet, Merchant of Venice\n ● Salman Rushdie: The Satanic Verses, Midnight's Children · Machiavelli: The Prince\n ● Hitler: Mein Kampf · Jane Austen: Pride and Prejudice · Leo Tolstoy: War and Peace, Anna Karenina\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Aristophanes ≠ Aristotle\" naam-trick\n Aristophanes aur Aristotle DONO Greek naam \"Aristo-\" se shuru hote hain isliye exam mein confuse karte hain — par\n Aristophanes ek PLAYWRIGHT hai(Lysistrata, The Clouds jaisi comedy plays likhi), jabki Aristotle ek PHILOSOPHER\n hai(Politics, Ethics jaisi kitaabein). Yaad rakho: \"Aristo-PHANES = PHANtasy/plays, Aristo-TLE = Theory/philosophy\" —\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 9 · Authors and Their Books\n\n suffix se hi field pehchano.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n \"Lysistrata\", \"Plutus\", aur \"The Clouds\" ARISTOPHANES ke plays hain, philosopher Aristotle ke nahi — dono similar-\n sounding naam ki wajah se frequently confuse hote hain.\n\n\n\n6. Autobiographies — Steve Jobs Biography-vs-Autobiography Trap\n ● Walter Isaacson: \"Steve Jobs\" — yeh BIOGRAPHY hai(kisi aur ne likhi), AUTOBIOGRAPHY nahi\n ● APJ Abdul Kalam: Wings of Fire · Nehru: An Autobiography · Gandhi: The Story of My Experiments with Truth\n ● Nelson Mandela: Long Walk to Freedom · Malala Yousafzai: I am Malala · Michelle Obama: Becoming\n ● Barack Obama: A Promised Land · Anne Frank: Diary of a Young Girl\n ● Dalai Lama: Freedom in Exile · Nirad C. Chaudhuri: The Autobiography of an Unknown Indian\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Isaacson ne likha, Jobs ne nahi\" trick\n \"Steve Jobs\" kitaab ka naam \"autobiography\" jaisa lagta hai(kyunki title mein sirf Jobs ka naam hai, \"my life\" jaisa kuch\n nahi) par ye AUTHOR Walter Isaacson hai, na ki Steve Jobs khud. Yaad rakho: \"Jab AUTHOR ka naam SUBJECT se ALAG\n ho, wo BIOGRAPHY hai\" — is chapter ki baaki saari kitaabein khud subject ne likhi hain(self-written), ye ek EXCEPTION\n hai jo list mein galti se \"autobiography\" jaisa dikh jaata hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Walter Isaacson ki \"Steve Jobs\" ek BIOGRAPHY hai(kisi aur ne likhi hai), autobiography nahi — commonly true\n autobiographies ke saath list ki jaati hai lekin technically yeh alag genre hai.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Kalidasa's Big-3: Shakuntalam(drama)-Raghuvansham(epic)-Meghasandesam(lyric) → Vande\n Mataram=Anandamath ka hissa(alag book nahi) → Tharoor: Era of Darkness(India)=Inglorious Empire(UK) → Sports:\n signature-title-career match → Aristophanes(playwright)≠Aristotle(philosopher) → Steve Jobs=Isaacson ki Biography,\n not autobiography\"\n\n\n                           Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) \"Vande Mataram\" Anandamath(Bankim Chandra) ke ANDAR hai — alag standalone book nahi hai.\n 2) Aristophanes(Lysistrata,Plutus,The Clouds ke playwright) aur philosopher Aristotle bilkul ALAG log hain — naam-\n similarity se confuse mat ho.\n 3) Walter Isaacson ki \"Steve Jobs\" ek BIOGRAPHY hai (author alag, subject alag) — autobiography nahi.\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 9 · Authors and Their Books\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.9 Authors and Their Books\n\n\n\n\n                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 10 · Awards\n\n                           AWARDS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 10 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (awarding body ka odd-one-out, similar-\nnaam wale alag awards, naam-badlaav wale awards), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Nobel Prize — Peace Ka Norwegian-Odd-One-Out\n  ● Nobel Foundation(1900) · Har saal 10 December ko award(Alfred Nobel ki death anniversary)\n  ● Awarding bodies: Royal Swedish Academy(Physics,Chemistry,Economics) · Karolinska Institute(Medicine) ·\n  Swedish Academy(Literature)\n  ● Peace Prize = SIRF ye Norwegian Nobel Committee dwara diya jaata hai — baaki sab SWEDISH\n  ● Raman(1930,Physics,Raman Effect) vs Chandrasekhar(1983,Physics,Chandrasekhar Limit) — dono Physics, alag\n  discoveries\n  ● 2024: Peace-Nihon Hidankyo · Physics-Hopfield&Hinton · Literature-Han Kang\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"4 Swedish, 1 Norwegian\" trick\n 4 category(Physics,Chemistry,Medicine,Literature) SWEDEN se award hoti hain, par PEACE akela alag desh — NORWAY\n se. Yaad rakho: \"Peace ka safar Sweden se Norway\" — Alfred Nobel khud Swedish the, par unhone specifically Peace\n Prize Norway ko diya kyunki tab Norway-Sweden ek union mein the, aur Norway ki international-diplomacy reputation\n thi. Raman aur Chandrasekhar dono PHYSICS mein jeete — par 53 saal ka gap(1930 vs 1983) aur alag discoveries(Effect\n vs Limit) — inhe merge mat karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Peace Prize ekmatra Nobel Prize hai jo ek Norwegian body(Norwegian Nobel Committee) dwara diya jaata hai — baaki\n sab Swedish institutions hain. Yeh bahut frequently poocha jaata hai.\n\n\n\n2. Pulitzer & Booker — Regular vs International Booker Trap\n  ● Pulitzer: Columbia University(1917), Joseph Pulitzer ki memory mein · First Indian: Gobind Behari Lal(1937)\n  ● Booker Prize: English-ORIGINAL novels ke liye · 2024 Winner: Samantha Harvey — 'Orbital'\n  ● Indian-origin Booker winners: Naipaul(1971), Rushdie(1981), Roy(1997), Kiran Desai(2006), Adiga(2008)\n  ● International Booker Prize: TRANSLATED fiction ke liye(author+translator dono credited), 2019 se\n  ● 2022 Indian Winner: Geetanjali Shree(Tomb of Sand) · 2025: Banu Mushtaq + translator Deepa Bhasthi(Heart\n  Lamp)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Regular=Original, International=Translated\" trick\n Booker Prize(regular) = sirf ENGLISH mein ORIGINAL likhi novel ke liye — akela author credit milta hai. International\n Booker = koi bhi language mein likhi novel jo ENGLISH mein TRANSLATE hui ho — author AUR translator dono credit\n milte hain(jaise Geetanjali Shree+Daisy Rockwell, Banu Mushtaq+Deepa Bhasthi). Yaad rakho: \"Regular=Solo credit,\n International=Duo credit(writer+translator)\" — dono naam ek saath yaad rakhna hi is category ka signature hai.\n\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 10 · Awards\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n International Booker Prize TRANSLATED fiction ke liye hai(author+translator dono credited); regular Booker Prize sirf\n English-original novels ke liye hai. In dono categories ko confuse mat karo.\n\n\n\n3. Magsaysay, Oscar & Grammy — First Indian Winners\n ● Ramon Magsaysay(1957) — \"Nobel Prize of Asia\" · First Indian: Vinoba Bhave(1958)\n ● Oscar(1929, National Academy of Motion Pictures) — First Indian: Bhanu Athaiya(Costume Design, \"Gandhi\")\n ● Satyajit Ray: Oscar Lifetime Achievement(1992)\n ● Grammy(1958, National Academy of Recording Arts) — Indian record: Pt. Ravi Shankar(5×), Zakir Hussain(4×)\n ● 2025: Oscar Best Film-Anora · Grammy Best Global Music Album-Kendrick Lamar('Not Like Us')\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Bhave-Asia-Award, Athaiya-Costume, Shankar-Sitar\" first-trick\n Teen \"first Indian\" ek-line mein yaad karo: Vinoba Bhave = MAGSAYSAY ka first Indian(1958, samaj-seva). Bhanu\n Athaiya = OSCAR ka first Indian(costume design, Gandhi film). Ravi Shankar = GRAMMY mein sabse zyada baar jeetne\n wala Indian(5 baar, sitar-legend). Yaad rakho: \"Bhave-Athaiya-Shankar\" teen alag awards, teen alag fields(seva-\n costume-music) — first mein confuse mat karo.\n\n\n\n4. Bharat Ratna 2024 — 5 Recipients, 4 Posthumous\n ● Bharat Ratna(1954) — Peepal Leaf shape, Bronze, \"Satyameva Jayate\" inscribed\n ● First recipients(1954): Rajagopalachari, Radhakrishnan, C.V. Raman\n ● First posthumous: Lal Bahadur Shastri(1966) · Youngest: Sachin Tendulkar(2014)\n ● Foreign recipients: Khan Abdul Ghaffar Khan, Nelson Mandela\n ● 2024(5 recipients): Karpoori Thakur, Charan Singh, Narasimha Rao, Swaminathan — sab POSTHUMOUS. L.K.\n Advani — ZINDA\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"2024 mein 4 mare, 1 zinda\" trick\n 2024 ke 5 Bharat Ratna recipients mein se sirf EK zinda tha jab award mila — L.K. Advani. Baaki CHAARO(Karpoori\n Thakur, Charan Singh, Narasimha Rao, Swaminathan) POSTHUMOUS mile. Yaad rakho: \"Advani Akela Alive\" — A-A\n pattern se yaad rakho, baaki sab posthumous list hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n 2024 ke paanch Bharat Ratna recipients mein se, sirf L.K. Advani ne isse zinda rehte hue receive kiya — baaki chaar\n posthumous the. Ek common detail-check trap.\n\n\n\n5. Gallantry Awards — Precedence Order Chain\n ● Wartime order: Param Vir Chakra(1st) → Mahavir Chakra(2nd) → Vir Chakra(3rd)\n ● Peacetime: Ashoka Chakra → Kirti Chakra → Shaurya Chakra\n ● FULL precedence: PVC → Ashoka Chakra → Mahavir Chakra → Kirti Chakra → Vir Chakra → Shaurya Chakra\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 10 · Awards\n ● First PVC: Major Somnath Sharma(1949)\n ● National Film Awards(1954): 71st(2025) — Best Actor: SRK/Vikrant Massey · Best Film: 12th Fail\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"PAM-KVS\" precedence chain\n Full order yaad rakho: Param Vir(highest,PVC) → Ashoka Chakra(peacetime ka highest) → Mahavir Chakra → Kirti\n Chakra → Vir Chakra → Shaurya Chakra(sabse neeche). Bolo: \"P-A-M-K-V-S\" — yaad rakho \"PVC ke baad turant Ashoka\n Chakra aata hai\" (peacetime ka sabse bada wartime ke 2nd number ke barabar rank karta hai) — ye hi sabse zyada\n exam mein confuse hone wala step hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Order of precedence: Param Vir Chakra → Ashoka Chakra → Mahavir Chakra → Kirti Chakra → Vir Chakra → Shaurya\n Chakra. Ashoka Chakra(peacetime) PVC ke turant baad aata hai — is sequence mein Ashoka Chakra ki position bhool\n jaana common galti hai.\n\n\n\n6. Literary Awards — Saraswati Samman vs Vyas Samman\n ● Jnanpith(1965) — 22 Scheduled languages ke liye · First: G. Shankar Kurup(Malayalam,1965)\n ● Sahitya Akademi(1954) — 24 languages, LAST 5 SAAL ki composition ke liye\n ● Saraswati Samman(1991, K.K. Birla Foundation) — 8th Schedule ki KISI BHI language mein, pichhle 10 saal ki\n work\n ● Vyas Samman(1991, K.K. Birla Foundation) — SIRF HINDI writing ke liye\n ● Moortidevi Award(1983, Jnanpith Trust) — Indian language ya English literature ke liye\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Saraswati=Saari Bhasha, Vyas=Sirf Hindi\" trick\n Saraswati Samman aur Vyas Samman DONO 1991 mein, DONO K.K. Birla Foundation ne banaye — par scope alag:\n Saraswati = KISI BHI Indian language(8th Schedule) ke liye. Vyas = SIRF Hindi ke liye. Yaad rakho: \"Saraswati=Saari\n bhasha ki devi(all languages), Vyas=Hindi ke Mahabharata-writer(Hindi-specific feel)\" — same year, same foundation,\n alag scope.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Saraswati Samman aur Vyas Samman dono 1991 mein SAME foundation(K.K. Birla) dwara established kiye gaye —\n lekin Saraswati Samman kisi bhi Indian language ko cover karta hai, jabki Vyas Samman sirf Hindi ke liye hai.\n\n\n\n7. Science & Sports Awards — Khel Ratna Naam-Badlaav\n ● Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna(1991–92) — PEHLE naam \"Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna\" tha — India ka highest\n sporting honour\n ● Arjuna Award(1961) — 4-saal consistent performance · Dronacharya Award(1985) — coaches ke liye\n ● Khel Ratna 2024: Gukesh D(Chess), Praveen Kumar(Para-Athletics), Harmanpreet Singh(Hockey), Manu\n Bhaker(Shooting)\n ● Homi Bhabha Award(1990,nuclear) · Vikram Sarabhai Award(1990,space) · Borlaug Award(1972,agriculture)\n ● G.D. Birla Award(1991) — Indian scientists BELOW 50 years ke liye\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 10 · Awards\n\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Rajiv Gandhi se Dhyan Chand tak\" naam-badlaav trick\n India ka HIGHEST sporting award ka naam BADAL gaya hai — pehle \"Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna\" tha, ab \"Major Dhyan\n Chand Khel Ratna\" hai. Yaad rakho: \"Naam badla, award wahi hai\" — agar exam purana naam(Rajiv Gandhi Khel\n Ratna) poochhe ya naya(Dhyan Chand), dono SAME award hain. Purane naam ko galat mat samjho.\n\n\n\n8. Art & Rajiv/Indira Gandhi Award-Series\n ● Sangeet Natak Akademi Awards(1952) — Music, Dance, Theatre, Folk/Tribal Arts\n ● Rajiv Gandhi Environment Award — Clean technology adoption(industries)\n ● Indira Gandhi National Integrity Award — National unity/integrity\n ● Indira Gandhi Paryavaran Puraskar — Environment contribution\n ● Rajiv Gandhi Quality Improvement Award — Bureau of Indian Standards dwara\n ● Indira Priyadarshini Vriksha Mitra Award — Tree plantation/wasteland development\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Rajiv=Tech/Quality, Indira=Nature/Unity\" naam-split trick\n 6 alag Gandhi-family-naam-wale awards hain, par PATTERN se yaad rakho: RAJIV GANDHI wale awards =\n TECHNICAL/quality-focused(Environment-tech, Quality Improvement). INDIRA GANDHI wale awards = NATURE/unity-\n focused(National Integrity, Paryavaran, Vriksha Mitra-tree). Yaad rakho: \"Rajiv=Engineer-jaisa(tech/quality),\n Indira=Mother-Earth-jaisi(nature/unity)\" — naam dekh ke hi category-guess kar sakte ho.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Nobel: 4-Swedish+1-Norwegian(Peace) → Booker(original,solo) vs International Booker(translated,duo) → First\n Indians: Bhave(Magsaysay)-Athaiya(Oscar)-Shankar(Grammy) → Bharat Ratna 2024: Advani-akela-alive, baaki-\n posthumous → Gallantry: PVC-Ashoka-Mahavir-Kirti-Vir-Shaurya → Saraswati(saari-bhasha) vs Vyas(sirf-Hindi) →\n Khel Ratna: Rajiv-Gandhi-se-Dhyan-Chand naam-badla → Rajiv(tech/quality) vs Indira(nature/unity) awards\"\n\n\n                         Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Nobel Peace Prize = ekmatra Norwegian body(Norwegian Nobel Committee) dwara — baaki sab Swedish\n institutions.\n 2) International Booker = TRANSLATED fiction(author+translator dono credit). Regular Booker = English-ORIGINAL\n novels only.\n 3) Saraswati Samman = kisi bhi Indian language ke liye. Vyas Samman = SIRF Hindi ke liye — dono same year, same\n foundation, alag scope.\n\n\n                       Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.10 Awards\n\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 11 · Sports Panorama\n\n                SPORTS PANORAMA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 11 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (similar-sounding events jaise World Cup vs\nWorld Championship, format-specific terminology, first-edition traps), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye\ndimaag mein.\n\n1. Olympics Overview — Ring Colours + First-Editions\n  ● Origin: 776 AD(Olympia, Greece) · Modern Olympics: 1896 AD(Athens, Greece)\n  ● Motto: Citius(Faster) | Altius(Higher) | Fortius(Stronger) | Communiter(Together)\n  ● First Winter Olympics: Chamonix(1924) · First Paralympics: Rome(1960) · First Youth Olympics: Singapore(2010)\n  ● Ring colours by continent: Blue=Europe, Yellow=Asia, Black=Africa, Green=Australia, Red=Americas\n  ● London aur Paris — dono ne Olympics 3-3 baar host kiya, joint record · 2028: Los Angeles\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"BYBGR\" ring-continent trick\n 5 rings, 5 continents: Blue(Europe) → Yellow(Asia) → Black(Africa) → Green(Australia) → Red(Americas) = \"B-Y-B-G-R\".\n Yaad rakho: \"Bhai Yaar Bata Gaya Rasta\" ek silly line bana lo apni bhasha mein. London-Paris dono 3-3 baar host kar\n chuke hain — ye joint-record hai, ek ko dusre se zyada mat samjho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n London aur Paris dono ne Olympics ko TEEN-teen baar host kiya hai — sabse zyada hostings ka joint record. Ek shehar\n ko akela winner mat samjho.\n\n\n\n2. Indian Olympic Medalists — Sindhu Aur Chopra Ke Double-Medal\n  ● PV Sindhu: Silver(Rio 2016) + Bronze(Tokyo 2020) — DO individual medals, first Indian woman aisa karne wali\n  ● Neeraj Chopra: Gold(Tokyo 2020) + Silver(Paris 2024) — javelin mein dono baar podium\n  ● KD Jadhav: Bronze(Helsinki,1952) — independent India ka first individual Olympic medal\n  ● Abhinav Bindra: Gold(Beijing,2008) — 10m Air Rifle\n  ● Paris 2024: Men's Hockey-Bronze, Manu Bhaker-2 Bronze(individual+team)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Sindhu-2-Racket, Chopra-2-Javelin\" trick\n Do players ke paas DO-DO Olympic medals hain, alag-alag Olympics mein: Sindhu(Rio-Silver, Tokyo-Bronze — dono\n badminton) aur Chopra(Tokyo-Gold, Paris-Silver — dono javelin). Yaad rakho: \"Sindhu ka rank Silver-se-Bronze\n GIRA(downgrade), Chopra ka rank Gold-se-Silver GIRA\" — dono ka pattern same hai(pehla medal behtar, dusra thoda\n kam), is symmetry se dono yaad rakho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n PV Sindhu ke DO Olympic medals hain — Silver(Rio 2016) aur Bronze(Tokyo 2020) — isse woh do individual Olympic\n medals waali first Indian woman ban gayi. Neeraj Chopra ke bhi do hain: Gold(Tokyo 2020) aur Silver(Paris 2024).\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 11 · Sports Panorama\n3. Commonwealth Games & Cricket — Multiple \"First World Cup\" Trap\n ● CWG Origin: 1930(Hamilton, Canada) · India ne pehli baar 1934(London) participate kiya\n ● India ne 2010 CWG host kiya(2nd position finish) · Sabse zyada hosting: Australia(5 baar)\n ● First Men's Cricket World Cup(1975,England) — Winner: West Indies\n ● First Women's Cricket World Cup(1973,England) — Winner: England — MEN se 2 saal PEHLE shuru hua\n ● First T20 World Cup(2007,South Africa) — Winner: India · First WTC(2019–21) — Winner: New Zealand\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Women pehle, Men baad mein\" cricket-history trick\n Women's Cricket World Cup(1973) MEN's Cricket World Cup(1975) se 2 SAAL PEHLE shuru hua tha — log ulta sochte\n hain ki Men's pehle shuru hua hoga, par WOMEN's format hi PEHLA tha. Yaad rakho: \"W before M\" — Women's-1973,\n Men's-1975, seedha 2-saal ka gap. First T20 WC(2007) mein INDIA winner tha — Men's ODI World Cup format se bilkul\n alag pehla-winner.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n First Women's Cricket World Cup(1973, England) MEN's World Cup(1975) se PEHLE shuru hua — log isse ulta samajh\n lete hain. First T20 World Cup(2007) ka winner INDIA tha, jabki First ODI World Cup(1975) ka winner West Indies tha\n — mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n4. Hockey & Football — Blue Line Ka Ice-vs-Field Trap\n ● First Hockey World Cup(1971,Barcelona) — Winner: Pakistan(max 4 baar) · Playing time: 70 min, 11 players\n ● \"Blue Line\" = ICE hockey ka term hai, FIELD hockey ka NAHI\n ● Indian Men's Hockey team: 12 Olympic medals(8 Gold) · Wizard of Hockey: Dhyan Chand\n ● First FIFA World Cup(1930) — Winner: Uruguay · FIFA WC 2022(Qatar) — Winner: Argentina\n ● Most FIFA WC wins: Brazil(5 times) · Ballon d'Or 2024: Rodri(male), Bonmatí(female)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Blue Line = Ice, Field mein nahi\" trick\n \"Blue Line\" sirf ICE HOCKEY mein hota hai(rink pe drawn boundary-lines) — FIELD hockey(jo India khelta hai) mein ye\n term EXIST nahi karta. Yaad rakho: \"Blue=Barf(ice) ka rang jaisa\" — jab bhi \"blue line\" sawaal mein aaye, socho \"barf\n pe khelte hain\" — turant Ice Hockey confirm ho jaata hai, Field Hockey nahi.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n \"Blue Line\" term ICE hockey ka hai, field hockey ka NAHI — dono hockey formats ke beech ek frequent mix-up.\n\n\n\n5. Badminton & Tennis — Grand Slam Chronological Order\n ● Grand Slam chronological ORDER(calendar-wise): Australian Open → French Open → Wimbledon → US Open\n ● Wimbledon(1877,UK,Grass) — OLDEST Grand Slam by founding-year\n ● Australian Open(1905) — sabse NAYA founding mein, par calendar mein PEHLE khela jaata hai\n ● Thomas Cup(Men)/Uber Cup(Women) 2024 — China ne DONO jeete\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 11 · Sports Panorama\n ● Wimbledon 2025 mein electronic line calling introduce hui — pehli baar line judges replace hue\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Founding-order ≠ Calendar-order\" trick\n Do alag \"order\" hain jo confuse hoti hain: FOUNDING order(kab shuru hui) — Wimbledon(1877,oldest) → US\n Open(1881) → French Open(1891) → Australian Open(1905,newest). CALENDAR order(saal mein kab khelte hain) —\n Australian Open(Jan,pehle) → French Open → Wimbledon → US Open(baad mein). Yaad rakho: \"Australian sabse NAYI\n banी thi, par saal mein sabse PEHLE khelti hai\" — is paradox ko lock karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Grand Slam CALENDAR order: Australian Open → French Open → Wimbledon → US Open. Ye FOUNDING order se\n ALAG hai(Wimbledon 1877 mein sabse pehle bani thi) — dono orders ko mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n6. Table Tennis & Chess — Gukesh Ka World Championship vs World Cup\n ● Table Tennis(ITTA,1926) — Corbillon Cup(Women), Swaythling Cup(Men)\n ● FIDE Chess World Cup(har 2 saal) 2023 — Winner: Magnus Carlsen · Runner-up: R. Praggnanandhaa(India)\n ● Chess World CHAMPIONSHIP 2024(alag event) — Winner: D. Gukesh(India)\n ● FIDE Women's Chess World Cup 2025 — Winner: Divya Deshmukh · Runner-up: Koneru Humpy(dono India)\n ● Chess: 16 pieces per side · King=1-step-4-directions, Rook=straight(Hindi mein \"Elephant\")\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"World Cup ≠ World Championship\" trick\n Chess mein DO ALAG events hain jinke naam similar lagte hain: WORLD CUP(2-saal ka knockout tournament — 2023\n Carlsen jeete) vs WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP(alag format, title-match — 2024 Gukesh jeete). Yaad rakho:\n \"Cup=Tournament(bahut players), Championship=Title-Match(sirf 2 top players face-off karte hain)\" — Gukesh ka\n 2024 win WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP hai, World Cup nahi.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n D. Gukesh(World Championship 2024) aur Divya Deshmukh(Women's World Cup 2025) ALAG titles/events hain —\n World Championship ko World Cup format ke saath confuse mat karo.\n\n\n\n7. Nicknames, National Sports & Terminology — Complex-Sport Match\n ● Nicknames: P.T. Usha=Udanpari, K.D. Jadhav=Pocket Dynamo, Dravid=The Wall, Dhoni=Captain Cool\n ● National Sports: USA=Baseball, Canada=Ice Hockey, Japan=Judo, China=Table Tennis, France=Football,\n Malaysia=Badminton\n ● Complexes: Ring=Skating/Boxing, Pool=Swimming, Diamond=Baseball, Course=Golf, Rink=Ice Hockey,\n Track=Athletics\n ● Golf terms: Bogey, Bunker, Caddy, Putt, Tee · Boxing terms: Jab, Hook, Uppercut, Kidney Punch\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Complex-naam=Sport-hint\" trick\n Har sports-complex ka NAAM khud us sport ka hint deta hai — Diamond(shape wale field, baseball khelte hain) →\n                                       Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 11 · Sports Panorama\n\n Baseball. Rink(barf ki sheet) → Ice Hockey. Course(lamba ghumaav wala path) → Golf. Yaad rakho: \"Naam padho,\n shape socho, sport pata chal jaayega\" — is logic se ratt-na nahi padta, samajh se yaad ho jaata hai.\n\n\n\n8. Institutes & Other Facts — SAI Aur First-Records\n ● Sports Authority of India(SAI) — Established 1984, Societies Act 1860 ke under registered\n ● Nodal Ministry: Department of Sports, Ministry of Youth Affairs & Sports\n ● First Asian Kabaddi Championship(1980) · First Kabaddi World Cup: Mumbai(2004)\n ● Pro-Kabaddi League shuru hui 2014 mein · Calcutta Polo Club(1862) — duniya ka OLDEST polo tournament\n ● Anju Bobby George — first Indian athlete jisne World Athletics Championship medal jeeta(2003, France)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Kabaddi ka double-timeline\" trick\n Kabaddi ke DO alag milestones hain — Asian Championship(1980, sabse PEHLA continental event) aur World\n Cup(2004, Mumbai — 24 saal baad, GLOBAL level). Yaad rakho: \"1980=Asia-level shuru, 2004=World-level shuru\" —\n Pro-Kabaddi League(2014) is chain ka TEESRA/latest step hai — sequence: Asian(1980)→World Cup(2004)→Pro-\n League(2014), teeno alag scale ke events.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Olympics: BYBGR ring-colours → Sindhu(2 medals)-Chopra(2 medals) → Cricket: Women's WC(1973)-before-\n Men's(1975) → Blue Line=Ice Hockey only → Grand Slam: Founding-order(Wimbledon-oldest) vs Calendar-\n order(Australian-first) → Chess: World Cup(Carlsen)-vs-World Championship(Gukesh) → Complex-naam-se-sport-hint\n → Kabaddi: Asian(1980)-WorldCup(2004)-ProLeague(2014)\"\n\n\n                           Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Women's Cricket World Cup(1973) Men's(1975) se PEHLE shuru hua — log isse ulta samajh lete hain.\n 2) \"Blue Line\" sirf ICE hockey ka term hai, field hockey ka nahi.\n 3) Chess World Championship(2024,Gukesh) aur Chess World Cup(2023,Carlsen) ALAG events hain — format confuse\n mat karo.\n\n\n                    Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.11 Sports Panorama\n\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 12 · Indian Defence and Security\n\n    INDIAN DEFENCE AND SECURITY — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 12 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (similar-sounding organizations, cross-\nservice rank confusion, establishment-year traps), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Defence Structure & Ranks — Captain Ka Service-Wise Rank-Swap\n  ● Supreme Commander of Defence Forces: President of India · MoD head: Defence Minister\n  ● Department of Military Affairs — Head: Chief of Defence Staff(CDS). First CDS: Bipin Rawat, Current: Anil\n  Chauhan\n  ● DRDO(1958,New Delhi) — First Head: Dr. D.S. Kothari, Current: Dr. Samir V. Kamat\n  ● \"Captain\" — Navy mein SENIOR rank(Colonel ke barabar), Army mein JUNIOR rank\n  ● Top ranks: Field Marshal(Army) = Admiral of the Fleet(Navy) = Marshal of the Air Force(Air Force)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Captain-Navy-Bada, Captain-Army-Chota\" trick\n \"Captain\" SAME naam, par DONO services mein DIFFERENT seniority: Navy mein Captain ek SENIOR-level rank\n hai(Colonel ke barabar) jabki Army mein Captain ek JUNIOR-level rank hai(Lieutenant se thoda upar). Yaad rakho:\n \"Samundar mein Captain bada hota hai(jahaaz ka boss), zameen pe Captain chota hota hai(junior officer)\" — naam\n same, hierarchy alag, cross-service comparison mat karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n \"Captain\" different services mein alag rank levels denote karta hai — Navy mein ek senior rank(Colonel ke barabar)\n lekin Army mein ek junior rank. Branches ke beech equal seniority mat samajh lena.\n\n\n\n2. Commands & Training Institutes — NDA vs IMA Location Trap\n  ● National Defence Academy(NDA): Khadakwasla · Indian Military Academy(IMA): Dehradun\n  ● Officers Training Academy(OTA): Chennai · Infantry School: Mhow · School of Artillery: Deolali\n  ● Indian Naval Academy(INA): Ezhimala, Kerala · INS Chilka: Bhubaneswar, Odisha(seaman training)\n  ● Air Force Academy: Hyderabad · Paratroopers Training School: Agra\n  ● Har military command ka supreme officer \"Officer Commanding-in-Chief\" kehlata hai\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"NDA-Pune-side, IMA-Dehradun\" trick\n NDA(Khadakwasla, Pune ke paas) = TEENO forces(Army,Navy,Air Force) ke cadets ek saath training lete hain — \"Tri-\n service\" academy. IMA(Dehradun) = SIRF Army officers ke liye specific training. Yaad rakho: \"NDA=New-\n shuruaat(sabke liye common), IMA=India-Military-sirf-Army\" — NDA pehle jaate hain(joint), phir Army-bound cadets\n IMA jaate hain(specialized).\n\n\n\n3. Paramilitary Forces — Assam Rifles Ka Oldest-Force Trap\n  ● Assam Rifles(1835) — Bharat ka OLDEST paramilitary force, \"Sentinel of the North-East\"\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 12 · Indian Defence and Security\n ● CRPF(1939) — internal law and order mein assist karta hai — Assam Rifles se 104 saal BAAD bana\n ● BSF(1965) — International Borders guard karta hai · SSB(1963) — Nepal-Bhutan border guards\n ● NSG(1984) — \"Black Cat\", counter-terrorism · SPG(1985) — PM/ex-PM security\n ● RAF(1992) — CRPF ka specialised wing\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Assam Rifles 1835 = Sabse Purana\" trick\n CRPF ko log \"sabse purana/mashhoor\" samajh lete hain(kyunki wo sabse zyada visible/famous force hai) — par\n ACTUAL oldest paramilitary force ASSAM RIFLES hai(1835), jo CRPF(1939) se 104 SAAL PEHLE bani thi. Yaad rakho:\n \"Assam Rifles = 18-35(purana number), CRPF = 19-39(baad ka number)\" — fame se confuse mat ho, establishment-\n year hi sach batati hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Assam Rifles(1835) Bharat ka OLDEST paramilitary force hai — CRPF(1939) se kaafi purana, jise aksar wider recognition\n ki wajah se galti se oldest maan liya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n4. Defence PSUs — HAL vs MDL Headquarters Trap\n ● HAL(Hindustan Aeronautics Limited) — HQ: BENGALURU — Fighter aircraft, helicopters\n ● MDL(Mazagon Dock Shipbuilders) — HQ: MUMBAI — India's largest shipbuilder(1960 se govt-owned)\n ● BEL(Bharat Electronics): Bengaluru · BEML: Bengaluru · BDL(Bharat Dynamics): Hyderabad —\n Prithvi,Akash,Trishul,Nag missiles\n ● Garden Reach Shipbuilders: Kolkata · Goa Shipyard: Vasco da Gama, Goa\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"HAL-Airplane-Bengaluru, MDL-Dock-Mumbai\" trick\n HAL aur MDL ka naam-initial similar sound karta hai isliye confuse hote hain — HAL(AeronauticS/planes) BENGALURU\n mein hai(India ka tech-hub, aircraft-industry ke liye famous), MDL(Dock/ships) MUMBAI mein hai(India ka sabse bada\n PORT-city, isliye shipbuilding wahan). Yaad rakho: \"Plane=Bengaluru ki sky mein, Ship=Mumbai ke dock mein\" —\n geography-logic se match karo, sirf naam se confuse mat ho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n HAL ka headquarters BENGALURU mein hai, Mumbai mein NAHI — commonly MDL(Mazagon Dock) ke saath confuse\n kiya jaata hai, jo Mumbai mein hi headquartered hai.\n\n\n\n5. Missile Development — Prithvi vs Agni Range Ki Seedhi\n ● IGMDP(1983) — Father: Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam — 5 core missiles: Prithvi, Agni, Trishul, Akash, Nag\n ● Prithvi-I(1988,Chandipur) — 150km, FIRST INDIGENOUS missile · Prithvi-III(2009) — 350–600km\n ● Agni-I(1989) — 700–1200km(short) · Agni-V(2012) — 5000–8000km(inter-continental)\n ● BrahMos — India-Russia joint, naam DO nadiyon se(Brahmaputra+Moskva), \"Fire and Forget\"\n ● Sagarika/K-15 — India's first nuclear-capable SLBM(2008) · Astra — air-to-air missile\n\n\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 12 · Indian Defence and Security\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Prithvi=Chota-Range, Agni=Bada-Range\" trick\n PRITHVI(dharti/earth) = SHORT-range missiles(150–600km) — jaise zameen pe kaam ho. AGNI(fire) = LONG-range\n missiles(700km se 8000km+) — jaise aag door tak failti hai. Yaad rakho: \"Prithvi=Chhoti duniya(kam range),\n Agni=Poore continent tak(zyada range)\" — naam ka meaning hi range-scale ka hint deta hai. BrahMos ka naam trick:\n \"Brah\"=Brahmaputra(India), \"Mos\"=Moskva(Russia) — do desh, do nadi, ek missile.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n BrahMos ka naam DO rivers se aata hai: Brahmaputra(India) aur Moskva(Russia) — India-Russia joint development ko\n reflect karte hue. Prithvi-Agni ke ranges mix mat karo — Prithvi variants sabhi 600km ke andar hain, Agni variants\n 700km+ se shuru hote hain.\n\n\n\n6. Military Aircraft — Rafale Ki Speed-Range Numbers\n ● Tejas(HAL) — world's smallest/lightest multi-role supersonic aircraft\n ● Rafale(Dassault, France) — 4th-gen STEALTH, Speed:2222km/hr, Range:3700km\n ● Mirage 2000(Dassault, France) — Rafale se ALAG generation, multi-role fighter\n ● Sukhoi-30 MKI(Russia) — 12 missile types simultaneously fire kar sakta hai\n ● Dhruv — indigenous twin-engine helicopter, 14-seater · HTT-40 — indigenous basic trainer\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"France Ka Double\" trick\n France(Dassault Aviation) ke DO alag fighter aircraft India ke paas hain — Rafale(NEW-gen, stealth) aur Mirage\n 2000(OLDER-gen). Yaad rakho: \"Dassault = France ka aircraft-maker, do generation supply ki — Mirage pehle, Rafale\n baad mein aaya, dono ek hi French company se\". Rafale ke numbers ratt lo: \"22-22\"(speed km/hr) aur \"37-00\"(range\n km) — dono mein \"22\" aur double-zero pattern se yaad rakho.\n\n\n\n7. Warships & Submarines — Project 75 vs Project 17A\n ● Project 75 = SUBMARINES(Kalvari Class) — INS Kalvari, Khanderi, Karanj, Vela, Vagir, Vagsheer\n ● Project 17A = STEALTH FRIGATES(Nilgiri Class) — INS Nilgiri, Himgiri, Udaygiri, Dunagiri, Taragiri, Vindhyagiri\n ● INS Vikrant — India ka first INDIGENOUS aircraft carrier(2013 launched, Cochin Shipyard)\n ● INS Vikramaditya — Russia se PURCHASE ki gayi(2004), inducted 2013 — Vikrant se ALAG(purchased vs built)\n ● INS Arihant — India's first indigenous SUBMARINE(2016)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"75=Submarine, 17A=Frigate\" trick\n Project 75 aur Project 17A ke naam confuse karte hain — Project 75 = SUBMARINES(paani ke ANDAR chalti hain,\n Kalvari Class naam mein hi \"machli-jaisa\" feel hai). Project 17A = FRIGATES(paani ke UPAR chalte hain, Nilgiri Class —\n pahaad ka naam, land-jaisi feel). Yaad rakho: \"75=neeche(submarine), 17A=upar(frigate)\" — dono French/indigenous\n collaboration hai par vessel-type bilkul alag.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Project 75 = submarines(Kalvari Class, French collaboration). Project 17A = stealth frigates(Nilgiri Class). Submarine aur\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 12 · Indian Defence and Security\n\n frigate projects ko mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n8. Major Tanks — Arjun vs Muntra Ka Manned-Unmanned Trap\n ● Arjun Tank(DRDO,2004) — 360° targeting, range 2.5km, desert+swampy+riverine areas mein kaam karta hai\n ● Arjun Mark-II — naya version, 40% indigenous components\n ● Bhishma/T-90(Russia se purchase) — Avadi, Chennai mein manufacture hota hai, missile-range 4km\n ● Muntra Tank — India's FIRST UNMANNED tank(2017), variants: Muntra-S/M/N\n ● First indigenous 155mm gun(Bofors-type) — TATA Group ne manufacture ki, 40km range\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Muntra=Bina-Driver, Arjun=Sath-Driver\" trick\n Arjun aur Bhishma dono MANNED tanks hain(insaan andar baith ke chalata hai) — par MUNTRA India ka FIRST\n UNMANNED tank hai(remote/AI se control hota hai, koi driver andar nahi). Yaad rakho: \"Muntra = MAN nahi,\n TRA(remote-control jaisa) — bina driver wala akela tank\" — jab bhi \"unmanned\" ya \"driverless tank\" poochha jaaye,\n Muntra hi sahi answer hai.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Captain: Navy(senior)-Army(junior) → NDA(tri-service,Khadakwasla)-IMA(Army-only,Dehradun) → Assam\n Rifles(1835,oldest)-CRPF(1939) → HAL(planes,Bengaluru)-MDL(ships,Mumbai) → Prithvi(short-range)-Agni(long-\n range) → Rafale(new)-Mirage(older), dono France → Project 75(submarines)-17A(frigates) → Arjun(manned)-\n Muntra(unmanned)\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Assam Rifles(1835) = OLDEST paramilitary force, CRPF(1939) nahi — fame se confuse mat ho.\n 2) HAL(aircraft) HQ = Bengaluru. MDL(ships) HQ = Mumbai — dono ko swap mat karo.\n 3) Project 75 = SUBMARINES(Kalvari Class). Project 17A = FRIGATES(Nilgiri Class) — vessel-type mix mat karo.\n\n\n               Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.12 Indian Defence and Security\n\n\n\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 13 · Indian Nuclear Program\n\n        INDIAN NUCLEAR PROGRAM — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 13 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (similar-sounding reactors, first-vs-largest\ndistinctions, naam-swap traps), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Governing Bodies — Bhabha Ka Double-Hat\n  ● Father of Indian Nuclear Program: Dr. Homi J. Bhabha\n  ● Atomic Energy Commission(10 Aug 1948) — First Chairman: Dr. Homi J. Bhabha(bhi yahi vyakti)\n  ● Department of Atomic Energy(3 Aug 1954) — HQ: Mumbai, directly PM ke under\n  ● Atomic Energy Regulatory Board(15 Nov 1983) — safe/environmentally-friendly atomic energy use\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Bhabha ka Father-aur-Chairman Double-role\" trick\n Dr. Homi Bhabha DO title ek saath hold karte hain — \"Father of Indian Nuclear Program\"(overall credit) AUR \"Atomic\n Energy Commission ka FIRST Chairman\"(1948, official post). Yaad rakho: \"Bhabha = Pehle Commission banaya, phir\n khud uske Chairman bhi bane\" — dono roles same vyakti ko refer karte hain, exam alag options mein confuse kar\n sakta hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Dr. Homi J. Bhabha do \"first\" hats pehente hain: Father of the Indian Nuclear Program AND Atomic Energy Commission\n ke first Chairman(1948) — dono facts same vyakti ke hain.\n\n\n\n2. Research Centres — CIRUS Ka Spelling-Trap\n  ● BARC(1954, Trombay-Mumbai) — CIRUS Thermal Reactor Canada ke saath cooperation se bana\n  ● \"CIRUS\" = Canada-India Reactor, Utility Services — aksar galti se \"CYRUS\" likh diya jaata hai\n  ● UCIL(1969, Jadugoda-Jharkhand) — uranium mining/refining\n  ● IGCAR(1971, Kalpakkam-TN) — Fast Breeder Reactors ka R&D\n  ● NPCIL(1987, Mumbai) — nuclear power plants construction/operation\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"CIRUS = Canada-India, CYRUS Nahi\" spelling-lock\n CIRUS naam ek ACRONYM hai — Canada-India Reactor, Utility Services — jo Persian naam \"CYRUS\"(jaise Cyrus the\n Great) jaisa SOUND karta hai isliye log galat spelling likh dete hain. Yaad rakho: \"CIRUS = C-for-Canada, I-for-India\" —\n pehle do letters hi dono desh(joint-cooperation) bata rahe hain, isliye \"CYRUS\" nahi \"CIRUS\" sahi spelling hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n BARC mein Canadian cooperation se bana reactor CIRUS hai(Canada-India Reactor, Utility Services), jise commonly\n notes aur low-quality sources mein galti se \"CYRUS\" likh diya jaata hai — dono naam frequently confuse hote hain.\n\n\n\n3. Nuclear Reactors — Apsara vs Kamini Ka Do-Alag-First\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 13 · Indian Nuclear Program\n ● Apsara Reactor(1956) — ASIA mein FIRST reactor(overall)\n ● Kamini Reactor(1996) — duniya ka FIRST reactor jo URANIUM-233 fuel use karta hai; developing world ka first\n Fast Breeder Neutron\n ● CIRUS(1960) · Zerlina(1961) · Purnima(1972) · Dhruva(1985) · Apsara-U(2018, upgraded version)\n ● Yaad rakho: Apsara(1956) aur Apsara-U(2018) — 62 saal ka gap, ek hi naam ka upgraded version\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Apsara=Asia-first, Kamini=Fuel-first\" trick\n Do reactors, do ALAG \"first\" claims: Apsara(1956) = ASIA ka pehla reactor(continental-level first). Kamini(1996) =\n URANIUM-233 fuel use karne wala duniya ka pehla reactor(fuel-technology-level first). Yaad rakho: \"Apsara=Continent\n ka pehla, Kamini=Fuel-type ka pehla\" — dono \"first\" hain par scope bilkul alag, mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Apsara(1956) = Asia mein first reactor. Kamini(1996) = duniya ka first reactor jo Uranium-233 fuel use karta hai. Do\n alag \"firsts\" hain — inhe merge mat karo.\n\n\n\n4. Nuclear Power Plants — Tarapur(First) vs Kudankulam(Largest)\n ● First in India: Tarapur, Maharashtra(1969, US cooperation) — 1400 MWe\n ● Largest in India: Kudankulam, Tamil Nadu(2014) — 2000 MWe capacity\n ● First in World: Russia(Obninsk,1954) · Second in World: America(1958)\n ● Rawatbhata(Rajasthan,1973) · Kalpakkam(TN,1984) · Narora(UP,1991) · Kakrapar(Gujarat,1993) ·\n Kaiga(Karnataka,2000)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Tarapur=Pehla-Chota, Kudankulam=Naya-Bada\" trick\n Tarapur(1969) = FIRST hai(sabse purana, chronologically pehle) par CAPACITY mein chota(1400 MWe).\n Kudankulam(2014) = LARGEST hai(sabse zyada capacity, 2000 MWe) par sabse NAYA bhi hai. Yaad rakho: \"Jitna naya\n plant, utni zyada capacity\" — technology improve hui to naya plant bada bana, isliye first(purana) aur largest(naya) do\n alag jagah hain.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Tarapur Bharat ka FIRST nuclear power plant hai(1969) year ke hisaab se, lekin Kudankulam LARGEST hai capacity ke\n hisaab se(2000 MWe, 2014) — \"first\" ko \"largest\" ke saath confuse mat karo.\n\n\n\n5. Nuclear Tests & WWII — Hiroshima-Nagasaki Naam-Trap\n ● India's First Nuclear Test: 18 May 1974, Pokhran — \"Smiling Buddha\", 12 Kilotonnes\n ● India's Second Nuclear Test: 11 & 13 May 1998, Pokhran — \"Operation Shakti\"\n ● Hiroshima(6 August 1945) → bomb naam: \"Little Boy\"\n ● Nagasaki(9 August 1945) → bomb naam: \"Fat Man\"\n\n\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 13 · Indian Nuclear Program\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Little-Boy-Hiroshima-pehle, Fat-Man-Nagasaki-baad\" trick\n Bomb-naam aur city-naam ka koi logical connection nahi hai isliye exam swap kar deta hai — yaad rakho DATE se:\n Hiroshima PEHLE aaya(6 August) isliye \"Little\"(chota/pehla number jaisa) Boy uske saath. Nagasaki BAAD mein aaya(9\n August, 3 din baad) isliye \"Fat\"(bada number jaisa) Man uske saath. Bolo: \"Little pehle, Fat baad mein\" — date-\n sequence se naam-pairing lock karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Hiroshima → \"Little Boy\"(6 Aug); Nagasaki → \"Fat Man\"(9 Aug) — naam aur cities exams mein aksar swap kar diye\n jaate hain, isliye inhe date order se link karo.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Bhabha: Father + AEC first Chairman(1948) → CIRUS(Canada-India, not Cyrus) → Apsara(Asia-first,1956)-\n Kamini(Uranium-233-first,1996) → Tarapur(India's-first-plant,1969)-Kudankulam(largest,2014) → Nuclear tests:\n Smiling Buddha(1974)-Operation Shakti(1998) → Hiroshima(Little Boy,6Aug)-Nagasaki(Fat Man,9Aug)\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) CIRUS(Canada-India Reactor) ki spelling \"CYRUS\" nahi hai — C-for-Canada, I-for-India yaad rakho.\n 2) Tarapur = India ka FIRST nuclear power plant(1969, chota capacity). Kudankulam = LARGEST(2014, 2000 MWe) —\n first aur largest alag hain.\n 3) Hiroshima → \"Little Boy\"(6 Aug, pehle). Nagasaki → \"Fat Man\"(9 Aug, baad mein) — date-order se naam-pairing\n lock karo.\n\n\n                Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.13 Indian Nuclear Program\n\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 14 · Space Program in India\n\n          SPACE PROGRAM IN INDIA — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 14 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (similar-sounding \"firsts\", mission-vehicle\npairing, orbit-altitude confusion), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Overview — Sarabhai Ka Father-Aur-Chairman Combo\n  ● Space Program shuru: 1962 · Father of Indian Space Program: Vikram Sarabhai\n  ● Indian National Committee for Space Research(1962) — First Chairman: Vikram Sarabhai(bhi yahi vyakti)\n  ● ISRO Formed: 1969(HQ:Bengaluru) — Department of Space & Space Commission: 1972\n  ● National Space Day: 23 August — Chandrayaan-3 success ko mark karta hai\n  ● New Space India Limited(NSIL,2019) — ISRO ka COMMERCIAL arm\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Sarabhai = Bhabha jaisa Double-role\" trick\n Vikram Sarabhai bhi(nuclear-wale Bhabha ki tarah) DO title hold karte hain — \"Father of Indian Space Program\" AUR\n \"space-committee ke FIRST Chairman\"(1962). Yaad rakho: \"Sarabhai=Space ka Bhabha\" — dono field mein founder-\n cum-first-chairman pattern repeat hota hai, is parallel se dono chapters cross-link ho jaate hain.\n\n\n\n2. ISRO Space Centres — Bengaluru-Cluster Ka Group-Trick\n  ● Vikram Sarabhai Space Centre(1963, Thiruvananthapuram) — launch vehicle technology\n  ● Satish Dhawan Space Centre/SHAR(1971, Sriharikota) — ISRO's MAIN launch centre\n  ● ISAC(1972), ISTRAC(1976), LPSC(1987) — TEENO Bengaluru mein hain\n  ● Space Applications Centre(1972, Ahmedabad) · NRSC(1974, Hyderabad)\n  ● ISRO Propulsion Complex/IPRC(2014, Mahendragiri, TN) — cryogenic engine development\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Bengaluru-3\" cluster trick\n TEEN centres akele Bengaluru mein hain — ISAC(satellite design), ISTRAC(tracking), LPSC(liquid propulsion). Yaad\n rakho: \"Bengaluru = ISRO ka Brain-Cluster\" — teeno alag kaam karte hain(design-tracking-propulsion) par ek hi shehar\n mein. Baaki centres(VSSC-Thiruvananthapuram, SHAR-Sriharikota) alag-alag states mein hain, unhe individually yaad\n rakho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Zyada tar ISRO centres Bengaluru ke aas-paas cluster hote hain(ISAC, ISTRAC, LPSC) — in teeno ko \"Bengaluru group\"\n ke roop mein saath yaad rakho.\n\n\n\n3. Satellites & Orbits — LEO vs Geosynchronous Altitude-Trap\n  ● First Artificial Satellite(World): Sputnik-1(1957,USSR) · First Indian: Aryabhata(1975)\n  ● LEO(Low Earth Orbit) — Altitude ~200–2000km, remote-sensing ke liye use hota hai\n  ● Geosynchronous Orbit — Altitude 36,000km(BAHUT bada gap se LEO se), communication satellites ke liye\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 14 · Space Program in India\n ● Solar-Synchronous Orbit — 500–1000km, near-polar · Molniya Orbit — 504–39,834km(highly elliptical)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"LEO=Paas, Geo=Bahut Door\" altitude trick\n LEO aur Geosynchronous ke beech HUGE gap hai — LEO(2000km tak, Earth ke bahut kareeb, remote-sensing ke liye)\n vs Geosynchronous(36,000km, LEO se 18x zyada door, communication ke liye). Yaad rakho: \"LEO=Low(chota number),\n Geo=Ghana-door(bada number, 36-hazaar)\" — dono orbit-type ka KAAM bhi alag hai isse: paas wala\n orbit=dekhne(sensing) ke liye, door wala orbit=baat-cheet(communication) ke liye.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Geosynchronous orbit altitude(36,000km) ko LEO(200–2000km) ke saath aksar confuse kiya jaata hai — LEO Earth ke\n bahut kareeb hai(remote sensing ke liye), Geosynchronous communication satellites ke liye hai.\n\n\n\n4. World Space History — Country-Wise First-Satellite Dates\n ● 1957: Sputnik-1(USSR) — first artificial satellite EVER\n ● 1958: Explorer-1(USA) · 1969: Apollo-11(USA) — first human Moon-landing\n ● France: Astérix(1965) · Japan: Ohsumi(1970) · China: Dong Fang Hong-1(1970)\n ● UK: Prospero(1971) · India: Aryabhata-1(19 Apr 1975)\n ● Agencies: NASA(USA,1958), ESA(22-member,1975), JAXA(Japan,2003), CNES(France,1961)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"1957-58-65-70-70-71-75\" chronological satellite-chain\n Country-order chronologically: Russia(1957) → USA(1958) → France(1965) → Japan(1970) → China(1970, SAME saal\n Japan ke) → UK(1971) → India(1975). Yaad rakho: \"Cold-War superpowers pehle(Russia-USA), phir Europe(France),\n phir Asia(Japan-China), phir UK, phir India\" — India is list mein LAST hai(1975), sabse baad mein satellite launch karne\n wala major desh.\n\n\n\n5. Chandrayaan Missions — 1-2-3 Ka Vehicle-aur-Landing-Site Chain\n ● Chandrayaan-1(22 Oct 2008) — PSLV-C11, India's FIRST lunar mission\n ● Chandrayaan-2(22 Jul 2019) — GSLV-MkIII(\"Bahubali\"), South Pole target, PARTIALLY successful, impact point:\n Tiranga Sthal\n ● Chandrayaan-3(14 Jul 2023) — LVM3-M4, Lander:Vikram, Rover:Pragyan, landing site: Shiv Shakti Sthal\n ● Aditya L-1(2 Sep 2023) — PSLV-C57, India's FIRST mission to study Sun\n ● Gaganyaan — future MANNED mission · NISAR — joint NASA-ISRO LEO observatory\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"1-PSLV-Safal, 2-GSLV-Aadhi, 3-LVM3-Poora\" trick\n Teen Chandrayaan, teen alag launch-vehicle, teen alag outcome: Chandrayaan-1(PSLV, poori tarah safal-orbit mission)\n → Chandrayaan-2(GSLV-MkIII/Bahubali, PARTIALLY successful — lander crash hua par orbiter safal raha) →\n Chandrayaan-3(LVM3, POORI tarah safal — landing bhi hui). Yaad rakho: \"2 mein adhoora reh gaya kaam, 3 mein\n poora kiya\" — Tiranga Sthal(2's impact point) aur Shiv Shakti Sthal(3's landing site) ko alag rakho, dono alag missions\n ke naam hain.\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 14 · Space Program in India\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Chandrayaan-2 ka impact point \"Tiranga Sthal\" hai, Chandrayaan-3 ka landing site \"Shiv Shakti Sthal\" hai — dono ALAG\n naam, ALAG missions, mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n6. Astronauts — Rakesh Sharma vs Chawla vs Shukla Ka Triple-First\n ● First Indian Astronaut(citizen): Rakesh Sharma(1984, Soyuz T-11)\n ● First Woman of Indian ORIGIN in Space: Kalpana Chawla(1997,2003 — US citizen, Space Shuttle Columbia)\n ● Second Woman of Indian Origin: Sunita Williams(2006 — bhi US citizen)\n ● First Indian to reach ISS: Shubhanshu Shukla(Axiom Mission 4/Ax-4)\n ● Chawla aur Williams DONO Indian-origin(US citizens) hain — Rakesh Sharma genuinely Indian citizen the\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"3 Alag First, 3 Alag Qualifier\" trick\n Teen \"first\" hain, teen ALAG qualifiers ke saath: Rakesh Sharma = first INDIAN CITIZEN jo space gaya(1984). Kalpana\n Chawla = first Indian-ORIGIN(US-citizen) woman jo space gayi. Shubhanshu Shukla = first Indian jo specifically ISS(space\n station) pahuncha. Yaad rakho: \"Sharma=Citizen-first, Chawla=Origin-first(woman), Shukla=ISS-first\" — teeno qualifier\n alag hain, ek hi \"first Indian in space\" mat samjho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Kalpana Chawla aur Sunita Williams Indian-ORIGIN hain(US citizens); Rakesh Sharma genuinely Indian citizen the jo\n space mein gaye first the; Shubhanshu Shukla specifically ISS pahunchne waale first Indian hain. Teen alag \"firsts\" hain\n — inhe merge mat karo.\n\n\n\n7. Launch Vehicles — India Space Club Ka 6th-Member Order\n ● SLV-3(18 Jul 1980) — India's FIRST launch vehicle, India Space Club ka 6TH member ban gaya\n ● Order: USA → USSR → France → Japan → China → INDIA(6th)\n ● PSLV(20 Dec 1993) — ISRO's PRIMARY vehicle, 4-stage rocket, 400–900km, up to 1750kg\n ● GSLV — 36,000km tak, 3-stage, first launch FAILED(2001), first SUCCESS(8 May 2003)\n ● GSLV Mk III = \"Bahubali\" naam(heavy-lift capability) · AstroSat(2015) — India's first space observatory\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"USA-USSR-France-Japan-China-India\" 6th-member chain\n Space Club mein India 6TH member tha — order yaad karo: USA(1st) → USSR(2nd) → France(3rd) → Japan(4th) →\n China(5th) → INDIA(6th, 1980, SLV-3 ke saath). Yaad rakho: \"Superpowers pehle, phir Europe, phir Asia ke 3\n desh(Japan-China-India order mein)\" — India is club ka LAST/newest member tha jab join kiya.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n India Space Club mein SIXTH country tha — order tha USA, USSR(Russia), France, Japan, China, phir India(1980, SLV-3\n ke saath). Is list ki sahi sequencing ek common exam question hai.\n\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath                                             Static GK · Chapter 14 · Space Program in India\n\n\n\n\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Sarabhai: Father + Committee first-Chairman(1962) → Bengaluru-3: ISAC-ISTRAC-LPSC → LEO(2000km,paas)-\n Geo(36000km,door) → Satellite chain: Russia(57)-USA(58)-France(65)-Japan/China(70)-UK(71)-India(75) →\n Chandrayaan: 1(safal)-2(adhoora)-3(poora) → Astronauts: Sharma(citizen-first)-Chawla(origin-first)-Shukla(ISS-first)\n → Space Club 6th: USA-USSR-France-Japan-China-INDIA\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Geosynchronous orbit(36,000km) LEO(200–2000km) se BAHUT door hai — sensing ke liye LEO, communication ke\n liye Geo.\n 2) Rakesh Sharma(citizen-first), Kalpana Chawla(origin-first-woman), Shubhanshu Shukla(ISS-first) — teen ALAG\n \"firsts\", merge mat karo.\n 3) India Space Club ka 6TH member tha: USA-USSR-France-Japan-China ke BAAD(1980, SLV-3).\n\n\n                 Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.14 Space Program in India\n\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 15 · International Organization / Institution\n\n         INTERNATIONAL ORGANIZATIONS & INSTITUTIONS —\n                     MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 15 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (similar-sounding bodies jaise IMF-vs-World\nBank, same-city clusters, framework-vs-action treaties), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. UN & Organs — Trusteeship Ka Inactive-Not-Abolished Trap\n  ● UN established: 24 Oct 1945 · Founding members: 51(Poland 51st) · Members now: 193(South Sudan\n  193rd,2011)\n  ● 6 Organs: General Assembly, Secretariat, ECOSOC(54 members), Trusteeship Council, Security Council, ICJ\n  ● Security Council: 15 members — 5 Permanent(veto: USA,Britain,France,Russia,China) + 10 Non-Permanent\n  ● ICJ(The Hague) — 15 judges, 9-year term, 5 retire every 3 years\n  ● Trusteeship Council — technically STILL ek organ hai, par 1994 se INACTIVE(abolished nahi)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Inactive ≠ Abolished\" trick\n Trusteeship Council ko log \"khatam/abolished\" samajh lete hain — par ACTUALLY ye organ UN ke 6 organs mein AB\n BHI officially COUNT hota hai, sirf 1994 se koi kaam nahi kar raha(non-operational). Yaad rakho: \"Board pe naam hai,\n par duty pe nahi\" — jaise koi employee suspended ho par job-title abhi bhi list mein ho. \"6 organs\" poochha jaaye toh\n Trusteeship Council ko list se mat hataao.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Trusteeship Council technically ab bhi UN ka ek organ hai lekin 1994 se INACTIVE hai — isse \"abolished\" mat kaho, sirf\n non-operational hai.\n\n\n\n2. UN Agencies — Geneva Ka 5-Body Cluster\n  ● GENEVA mein: ITU(1865), ILO(1919), WMO(1950), WHO(1948), WIPO(1969) — 5 alag agencies\n  ● UNESCO(1945/46, Paris) — Educational,Scientific,Cultural\n  ● ICAO(1944, Montreal) — civil aviation, 193 members · IMO(1948, London) — navigation safety\n  ● UNICEF(1946, New York) · UNEP(1972, Nairobi) · UNWTO(1975, Madrid)\n  ● ILO ne 1969 mein Nobel Peace Prize jeeta tha\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Geneva-5\" elimination trick\n 5 major UN agencies GENEVA mein hain — ITU, ILO, WMO, WHO, WIPO. Yaad rakho: \"Geneva = Swiss-based UN-hub\"\n — jab bhi MCQ mein \"iski HQ kahan hai\" poochha jaaye aur options mein Geneva ho, in 5 naamon mein se koi bhi ho\n sakta hai. Elimination-technique: agar option mein Paris(UNESCO), London(IMO), ya New York(UNICEF) bhi ho, unhe\n pehle rule-out karo, phir Geneva-wale 5 mein se sahi answer dhoondo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 15 · International Organization / Institution\n\n Zyada tar UN agencies GENEVA mein headquartered hain(ITU, ILO, WMO, WHO, WIPO) — elimination-based MCQs ke\n liye ek common grouping fact.\n\n\n\n3. Financial Bodies — IMF vs World Bank Ka Function-Trap\n ● IMF(27 Dec 1945, Washington DC) — 191 members, MONETARY cooperation/stability, President: Kristalina\n Georgieva\n ● World Bank(1945, Washington DC) — 189 members, DEVELOPMENT LOANS provide karta hai, President: Ajay\n Banga\n ● WTO(1 Jan 1995, Geneva) — 166 members(Timor-Leste 166th) — trade rules/disputes\n ● ADB(1966, Manila) — 69 members · WIPO(1969, Geneva) — 193 members\n ● IMF aur World Bank DONO 1945 mein bane, DONO Washington DC mein — par kaam alag\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"IMF=Monetary-Doctor, World Bank=Loan-dene-wala\" trick\n IMF aur World Bank SAME saal(1945), SAME shehar(Washington DC) — isliye sabse zyada confuse hone wali jodi hai.\n Yaad rakho: \"IMF = Monetary-Doctor\"(currency/exchange-rate stability check karta hai, jaise doctor health check karta\n hai) vs \"World Bank = Loan-dene-wala\"(development projects ke liye paisa udhaar deta hai, jaise bank). IMF=Stability,\n World Bank=Funding — dono ka kaam alag hai bawajood same location ke.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n IMF aur World Bank DONO 1945 mein founded the, dono ka HQ Washington DC mein hai — lekin IMF\n monetary/financial stability ensure karta hai jabki World Bank development LOANS provide karta hai. Unke functions\n ko confuse mat karo.\n\n\n\n4. Regional Blocs — NAM Ke 5 Founding-Fathers\n ● NAM(1961) — Founders: Nehru(India), Sukarno(Indonesia), Tito(Yugoslavia), Nasser(Egypt), Nkrumah(Ghana) —\n 120 members\n ● BRICS(2009) — 11 members, 5 naye: Egypt, Iran, UAE, Ethiopia, Indonesia\n ● SCO(2001, Beijing) — 10 members, latest: Belarus · NATO(1949, Brussels) — 32 members, 32nd: Sweden\n ● SAARC(1985, Kathmandu) — 8 members · ASEAN(1967, Jakarta) — 10 members\n ● G20(1999) — 19 countries+EU+African Union · G7(1975) — 7 members:\n US,UK,Germany,Italy,Japan,Canada,France\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"NSTNN\" NAM founders chain\n 5 leaders, 5 desh — Nehru(India) → Sukarno(Indonesia) → Tito(Yugoslavia) → Nasser(Egypt) → Nkrumah(Ghana) = \"N-\n S-T-N-N\". Yaad rakho: \"Naye Saathi Tak Naye Neta\" — ek silly line se pehle-letter chain lock ho jaata hai. Ye \"5 leaders\"\n question har exam mein classic hai, purs-order mein ratt lo.\n\n\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 15 · International Organization / Institution\n5. Treaties — Vienna Convention vs Montreal Protocol Ka Framework-Action Trap\n ● Vienna Convention(1985) — ozone layer FRAMEWORK(general agreement)\n ● Montreal Protocol(1987) — Vienna Convention ke UNDER specific ACTION PLAN, ozone layer protect karta hai\n ● CTBT(1996) — all nuclear tests PROHIBIT karta hai, India IS NOT a signatory\n ● Paris Agreement(2015) — global warming 2°C se neeche, 1.5°C target\n ● NSG(1974–75) — 48 members, nuclear export control · ISA(2015, Gurugram) — India's concept(Modi), 120\n members\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Vienna=Rule-Book, Montreal=Action-Plan\" trick\n Vienna Convention aur Montreal Protocol DONO ozone layer ke liye hain isliye confuse hote hain — par Vienna(1985)\n = sirf FRAMEWORK/agreement(rules likhi gayi, koi specific target nahi), Montreal(1987) = uske 2 saal BAAD wo\n framework ka SPECIFIC action-plan(kaunse chemicals ban karne hain, timeline kya hai). Yaad rakho:\n \"Vienna=Vichar(idea/framework), Montreal=Mission(concrete action)\" — Vienna PEHLE(sochna), Montreal BAAD\n mein(karna).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Vienna Convention(1985) aur Montreal Protocol(1987) DONO ozone layer ko protect karte hain — Vienna Convention\n framework hai, Montreal Protocol iske under specific action plan hai. Inhe unrelated mat samjho.\n\n\n\n6. Agricultural Institutes — Crop-Specific Institute Match\n ● Central Rice Research Institute: Cuttack, Odisha · Central Potato Research Institute: Shimla\n ● Indian Institute of Sugarcane Research: Lucknow · National Sugarcane Breeding Institute: Coimbatore\n ● Central Tobacco Research Institute: Rajahmundry, AP · Central Coconut Research Institute: Kasaragod, Kerala\n ● National Coffee Research Institute: Chikmagalur, Karnataka · National Dairy Research Institute: Karnal, Haryana\n ● Indian Agricultural Research Institute(Pusa): New Delhi — sabse GENERAL/overall institute\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Crop-ki-jagah = Institute-ki-jagah\" geography-match trick\n Har crop-institute WAHI region mein hai jahan wo crop naturally UGTI hai — Rice(Cuttack,Odisha — dhaan ka belt),\n Coconut(Kasaragod,Kerala — coastal), Coffee(Chikmagalur,Karnataka — coffee-hills), Potato(Shimla — thandi jagah).\n Yaad rakho: \"Jahan crop paida hoti hai, wahi uska research-institute bhi hai\" — geography-logic se ratt-na kam ho\n jaata hai.\n\n\n\n7. Mining, Energy & Environment — Dehradun Ka 4-Institute Cluster\n ● DEHRADUN mein CHAAR institutions: Indira Gandhi National Forest Academy, Wildlife Institute of India, Central\n Forest Research Institute, Indian Institute of Petroleum Research\n ● National Metallurgical Laboratory: Jamshedpur, Jharkhand · Central Mining & Fuel Research Institute: Dhanbad,\n Jharkhand\n ● Central Leather Research Institute: Chennai · Central Salt & Marine Chemicals Research Institute: Bhavnagar,\n Gujarat\n ● Zoological Survey of India: Kolkata · National Environmental Engineering Research Institute: Nagpur\n                                       Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 15 · International Organization / Institution\n\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Dehradun = Forest-aur-Petroleum Hub\" cluster trick\n Dehradun akela 4 institutions ka ghar hai — 3 FOREST/wildlife-related(Forest Academy, Wildlife Institute, Forest\n Research Institute) + 1 PETROLEUM(Indian Institute of Petroleum Research, jo alag field hai par same shehar mein hai).\n Yaad rakho: \"Dehradun = Jungle-3 + Tel-1\" — jab bhi in 4 mein se koi naam poochha jaaye, location Dehradun hi\n hoga(petroleum-wala bhi, jo thoda odd lagta hai par same cluster mein hai).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Dehradun mein CHAAR environment/forest institutions hain — Indira Gandhi National Forest Academy, Wildlife\n Institute of India, Central Forest Research Institute, aur Indian Institute of Petroleum Research. Dehradun ko\n forestry/petroleum research hub ke roop mein yaad rakho.\n\n\n\n8. Defence & Other Institutions — Bengaluru-Group Repeat-Pattern\n ● HAL, BEML, ISRO, Indian Institute of Astrophysics — SAB Bengaluru, Karnataka mein\n ● DRDO: New Delhi(chapter 12 se bhi cross-check karo) · BDL: Hyderabad · Mazagon Dock: Mumbai\n ● Garden Reach Shipbuilders: Kolkata · National Institute of Oceanography: Goa\n ● National Institute of Ocean Technology: Chennai · Indian Institute of Skiing/Mountaineering: Gulmarg, J&K\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Bengaluru = Tech-aur-Defence Capital\" repeat-pattern\n Bengaluru ka pattern is chapter mein BHI repeat hota hai(jaise Chapter 12 mein HAL aur Chapter 14 mein ISRO-\n centres) — HAL, BEML, ISRO, Astrophysics Institute SAB ek hi shehar mein. Yaad rakho: \"Bengaluru = India ka Silicon-\n cum-Defence-Valley\" — jab bhi in naamon mein se koi location-question aaye, Bengaluru ek safe default-guess\n hai(BDL-Hyderabad aur Mazagon Dock-Mumbai ko exceptions ki tarah alag yaad rakho).\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Trusteeship Council(inactive,not abolished) → Geneva-5(ITU-ILO-WMO-WHO-WIPO) → IMF(monetary)-World\n Bank(loans) → NAM-5-founders: N-S-T-N-N → Vienna(framework)-Montreal(action) → Crop-institutes match\n geography → Dehradun(forest-3+petroleum-1) → Bengaluru(HAL-BEML-ISRO-Astrophysics)\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Trusteeship Council abolished NAHI hai — technically UN ka organ hai, sirf 1994 se inactive.\n 2) IMF(monetary stability) aur World Bank(development loans) — same-year(1945), same-city(DC), par function bilkul\n alag.\n 3) Vienna Convention(1985,framework) aur Montreal Protocol(1987,action-plan) — dono ozone-layer ke liye hain, ek\n dusre ke under hain.\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 15 · International Organization / Institution\nExam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.15 International Organization / Institution\n\n\n\n\n                                  Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 5","Static GK · Chapter 16 · Computer\n\n                        COMPUTER — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                      Static GK · Chapter 16 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (similar-sounding terms jaise RAM-vs-ROM,\napplication-specific shortcut behavior, mission-vs-component naam-trap), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye\ndimaag mein.\n\n1. Introduction & Generations — Babbage vs Turing Ka Father-Trap\n  ● Father of Computer: Charles Babbage · Father of MODERN Computer: Alan Turing\n  ● First calculating device: Abacus · First digital computer: ENIAC\n  ● 1st Gen(1940-56,Vacuum Tube) → 2nd(1956-63,Transistor) → 3rd(1964-71,IC/Silicon) → 4th(1971-\n  present,Microprocessor) → 5th(AI)\n  ● Third generation IBM 360 se shuru hui — key marker\n  ● By Size: Micro,Mini,Mainframe,Super · By Function: Analog,Digital,Hybrid\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Babbage=Original, Turing=Modern\" trick\n DO alag \"Father\" titles hain — Babbage(19th century, Analytical Engine banaya, MECHANICAL computing ka concept\n diya) vs Turing(20th century, Turing Machine/theoretical computer science, MODERN computing ka foundation). Yaad\n rakho: \"Babbage=Purana-Original-Father, Turing=Naya-Modern-Father\" — same field, do alag era, do alag titles, mix\n mat karo.\n\n\n\n2. Supercomputers & Components — Airawat vs El Capitan(India-vs-World)\n  ● Top Indian Supercomputer: Airawat(CDAC,Pune) — 2nd:Param Siddhi, 3rd:Pratyush\n  ● Top World Supercomputer: El Capitan(California,USA) — 2nd:Frontier, 3rd:Aurora System(sab USA)\n  ● 26 Sep 2024: PM Modi ne 3 PARAM Rudra supercomputers launch kiye + ArKa,Arunika HPC systems\n  ● CPU = \"Brain\" — Control Unit(CU) + Arithmetic Logic Unit(ALU) + Primary Storage\n  ● Input: Keyboard,Mouse,Scanner,OCR · Output: Printer,Monitor,Plotters,Speaker\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Airawat=India-No.1, El Capitan=World-No.1\" trick\n India ka NUMBER-1 supercomputer(Airawat) aur World ka NUMBER-1(El Capitan) — bilkul ALAG hain, India abhi\n world-top nahi hai. Yaad rakho: \"Airawat = Hindi mythology ka hathi(Indra ka vahan) — India ka pride\" vs \"El Capitan =\n California ka bada peak-naam — World ka champion\" — dono \"No.1\" hain par SCOPE alag(desh vs duniya).\n\n\n\n3. Memory & Hardware — RAM-Temporary vs ROM-Permanent\n  ● RAM(Random Access Memory) — TEMPORARY, VOLATILE(power jaane par data gayab)\n  ● ROM(Read Only Memory) — PERMANENT, NON-VOLATILE(power jaane par bhi data rehta hai)\n  ● 1024 pattern: Bit→Byte(8bits)→KB→MB→GB→TB→PB→EB — har step 1024 guna\n  ● Motherboard=main PCB · DMA=CPU-bypass data transfer · Cache Memory=CPU-Memory ke beech fast memory\n  ● Optical: CD/DVD/Blu-ray · Solid State: Pen Drive/Memory Card · Magnetic: HDD/Floppy/Tape\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 16 · Computer\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"RAM=Ret(bhool jaata), ROM=Rock(pakka)\" trick\n RAM = Volatile — \"Ret(sand) jaisa\" — hawa/power jaate hi ud jaata hai(data khatam). ROM = Non-Volatile —\n \"Rock(patthar) jaisa\" — permanent, kabhi nahi mitta. Yaad rakho: \"RAM=Ret(temporary), ROM=Rock(permanent)\" —\n 1024-pattern bhi lock karo: \"1024 hamesha next unit ka multiplier hai\" — 1000 nahi, 1024(2 ki power).\n\n\n\n4. Software & OS — F2 Rename Shortcut Aur Software-Types\n ● Windows mein rename shortcut: F2 · Booting = computer start/restart karna\n ● Single-user OS: MS-DOS, Windows 9x · OS Types: Batch, Time-Sharing, Distributed, Network, Multi-Tasking,\n Multi-Processing\n ● Utility Software: Disk Compression, Disk Cleaners, Disk Defragmenter, Text Editor, Anti-Virus\n ● Open Source: Linux, Firefox, Chrome, Opera — source code FREELY available\n ● DBMS = data-collection + query-execution manage karta hai\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"F2=Rename\" quick-lock\n F2 = Windows mein SIRF rename ke liye hai — ek simple, single-purpose shortcut, isliye alag se pakka yaad rakho: \"F-\n TWO = File ka naam NAYA(2nd naam)\" — F1 help hai, F2 rename hai, inhe function-number se lock karo taaki F5(jo\n Word/PowerPoint mein alag kaam karta hai) se confuse na ho.\n\n\n\n5. Programming & MS Office — F5 Ka Word-vs-PowerPoint Different-Behavior\n ● F5(Word) — Find & Replace/Go To window kholta hai\n ● F5(PowerPoint) — slide show START(beginning se) karta hai · Shift+F5 — current slide se start\n ● Compiler(poora code translate karke run) vs Interpreter(line-by-line execute)\n ● LISP=AI, COBOL=Business, FORTRAN=Mathematical, JAVA=Internet-based\n ● MS Word default font: Aptos(replaced Calibri, early 2024) · Excel default column width: 8 characters\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"F5 = App-ke-hisaab-se-Alag\" trick\n F5 SAME key, par DUSRA kaam karta hai application ke hisaab se — Word mein \"F5=Find\"(kuch DHOONDHNA),\n PowerPoint mein \"F5=Full-screen SHOW\"(kuch DIKHANA). Yaad rakho: \"Word=Dhoondhta hai(search),\n PowerPoint=Dikhata hai(display)\" — dono \"F\" se shuru hote hain, is verbal-hook se application-specific behavior yaad\n rakho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n F5 Word(Find & Replace/Go To khol deta hai) vs PowerPoint(slide show start karta hai) mein DIFFERENT kaam karta\n hai — same key, application ke hisaab se alag function.\n\n\n\n6. Networks & Internet — LAN vs MAN vs WAN Ka Coverage-Seedhi\n ● LAN — 1 Mile, 10-100 Mbps — School/office/campus level\n ● MAN — 50 km tak, 100Mbps-1Gbps — City/metro level\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 16 · Computer\n ● WAN — 1000 km tak, 1Gbps-100Gbps — Network-of-networks(sabse bada)\n ● WWW: Tim Berners-Lee ne 1989 mein banaya\n ● Protocols: TCP(control), IP(addressing), FTP(file-transfer), HTTP(web), SMTP(mail)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"LAN-Local, MAN-Metro, WAN-World\" scale-seedhi\n Teeno naam mein hi scope hai — LAN(Local=chota area), MAN(Metropolitan=city), WAN(Wide=sabse bada, deshon ke\n beech). Yaad rakho: \"L-M-W = Local-Metro-World\" seedha CHOTA se BADA jaate hain — coverage\n bhi(1mile→50km→1000km) aur speed-range bhi is order mein badhta jaata hai. Ek hi pattern, teeno cheezein saath\n yaad ho jaati hain.\n\n\n\n7. Mobile Gen & AI — 1G-se-5G Country-Year Chain\n ● 1G: Japan,1979(Analog) → 2G: Finland,1991(Digital) → 3G: Japan,2001(High-speed IP)\n ● 4G: Norway&Sweden,2009(broadband) → 5G: South Korea,2019(20Gbps)\n ● AI Origin: 1950s, Founder: John McCarthy\n ● ChatGPT(2022,OpenAI) → Gemini(2023,Google) → DeepSeek/Qwen3/Grok4(2025)\n ● Malware types: Viruses(damage), Worms(hide), Ransomware(ransom-demand), Trojan Horse(non-self-\n replicating), Spyware(monitor)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Japan-Finland-Japan-Norway-Korea\" mobile-gen chain\n Mobile-generations ka desh-pattern interesting hai — Japan DO baar aata hai(1G AUR 3G, dono alag saal mein: 1979\n aur 2001). Yaad rakho: \"Japan ne shuru bhi kiya(1G), beech mein bhi lead liya(3G)\" — baaki teen(2G-Finland, 4G-\n Norway/Sweden, 5G-South Korea) sab ALAG desh hain. Japan ka DOUBLE-appearance hi is chain ka sabse zyada\n confuse hone wala part hai.\n\n\n\n8. Robotics — Tianwen-1(Mission) vs Zhurong(Rover) Ka Naam-Trap\n ● Zhurong = China's Mars ROVER, jo Tianwen-1 MISSION ka PART tha — dono ALAG entities\n ● Rex — world's first bionic man · Kirobo — first talking robot in SPACE\n ● Sophia(Saudi Arabia) — humans se communicate karti hai · Vyommitra(ISRO) — half-humanoid, Gaganyaan\n Mission ke liye\n ● Mitra — India's FIRST humanoid robot · FEDOR — Russian humanoid robot\n ● Snake Robot, Daksha, Netra — DRDO ke defence-robots\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Tianwen=Safar, Zhurong=Yatri\" trick\n Tianwen-1 aur Zhurong ek dusre ke saath itne juda hain ki log inhe SAME cheez samajh lete hain — par Tianwen-1 =\n poori MISSION(safar/journey ka naam), Zhurong = us mission ka ROVER(jo Mars pe utra, yatri jaisa). Yaad rakho:\n \"Tianwen=Poori Trip ka naam, Zhurong=Trip mein jo vehicle gaya uska naam\" — mission aur uska ek component, do\n alag level ki cheezein.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n                                       Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 16 · Computer\n\n Tianwen-1 MISSION ka naam hai; Zhurong wo ROVER hai jo us mission ke part ke roop mein land hua — inhe same\n entity mat samjho.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Babbage(original-father)-Turing(modern-father) → Airawat(India-No.1)-El Capitan(World-No.1) → RAM(ret,volatile)-\n ROM(rock,permanent) → F2=Rename(single-purpose) → F5: Word(find)-PowerPoint(show) → LAN-MAN-WAN(local-\n metro-world) → Mobile-gen: Japan(1G+3G double)-Finland(2G)-Norway(4G)-Korea(5G) → Tianwen-1(mission)-\n Zhurong(rover)\"\n\n\n                         Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) F5 Word(Find & Replace) vs PowerPoint(slide show start) — same key, application ke hisaab se alag function.\n 2) RAM = Temporary/Volatile memory. ROM = Permanent/Non-Volatile — inhe swap mat karo.\n 3) Tianwen-1 MISSION ka naam hai; Zhurong wo ROVER hai jo us mission ka part tha — same entity mat samjho.\n\n\n                      Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.16 Computer\n\n\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 17 · UNESCO World Heritage Sites in India\n\n UNESCO WORLD HERITAGE SITES IN INDIA — MEMORY TRICK\n                       SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 17 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (same-year listing pairs, category-\nconfusion, multi-city shared fields), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Overview — 44 Sites Ka 35-7-1 Split\n  ● Total(July 2025): 44 sites — 35 Cultural + 7 Natural + 1 Mixed\n  ● Latest/44th: Maratha Military Landscapes of India(11 July 2025)\n  ● Mountain Railways(UNESCO): Kalka-Shimla Toy Train(2008) + Darjeeling Railway(1999)\n  ● Key numbers: 44-Total, 35-Cultural, 7-Natural, 1-Mixed\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"35-7-1 = C-N-M\" split-lock\n 3 category, 3 number — Cultural(35, sabse zyada) → Natural(7, kam) → Mixed(1, sirf ek). Yaad rakho: \"C-N-M = Chota-\n se-Chota hota gaya\"(35→7→1, ghatta hua funnel) — Mixed category sabse RARE hai(sirf 1 site), isliye jab bhi \"mixed\"\n poochha jaaye, seedha yaad aa jaana chahiye ki iska answer UNIQUE hai.\n\n\n\n2. Cultural Sites (North & East) — Agra Fort-Taj Mahal Same-Year Trap\n  ● Agra Fort(1983) aur Taj Mahal(1983) — DONO SAME YEAR, SAME STATE(UP) listed hue\n  ● Delhi: Humayun's Tomb(1993), Qutub Minar(1993), Red Fort Complex(2007)\n  ● Bihar: Mahabodhi Temple(2002), Nalanda Mahavihara(2016)\n  ● West Bengal: Darjeeling Railway(1999), Shantiniketan(2023)\n  ● Assam: Ahom Moidams(2024) — sabse NAYA cultural site\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Agra Fort = Taj Mahal, Twins-jaise\" trick\n Agra Fort aur Taj Mahal EK HI SAAL(1983) mein listed hue — log ek ko doosre se \"pehle\" maan lete hain, par ye\n WRONG hai, dono TWINS ki tarah same-year mein aaye. Yaad rakho: \"1983 mein UP ka DOUBLE-entry\" — Fatehpur\n Sikri(1986) inse ALAG saal mein hai, UP ke teen sites mein confuse mat ho: Agra Fort+Taj Mahal(1983,twins), Fatehpur\n Sikri(1986,alag).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Agra Fort aur Taj Mahal DONO 1983 mein listed hue the(same year, same state) — commonly ek ko doosre se pehle\n maan liya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n3. Cultural Sites (South & West) — Maharashtra Ka 6-Site Record\n  ● Maharashtra = SABSE ZYADA cultural sites(6): Ajanta, Ellora, Elephanta Caves, CST, Victorian Gothic Ensemble,\n  Maratha Military Landscapes(2025)\n  ● Ajanta Caves(1983) + Ellora Caves(1983) — bhi SAME year mein listed\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 17 · UNESCO World Heritage Sites in India\n ● Karnataka: Hampi(1986), Pattadakal(1987), Sacred Ensembles of Hoysalas(2023)\n ● Gujarat: Rani Ki Vav(2014), Historic Ahmedabad(2017), Dholavira(2021)\n ● MP: Khajuraho(1986), Sanchi(1989), Bhimbetka(2003)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Maharashtra=6, Champion-State\" trick\n Maharashtra akela 6 cultural sites ka RECORD-HOLDER hai — koi doosra state itne close nahi hai. Yaad rakho:\n \"Maharashtra = UNESCO ka Champion State\" — Ajanta-Ellora bhi(jaise Agra-Taj) SAME year(1983) mein hain, isliye\n Maharashtra mein DOUBLE-1983-pattern repeat hoti hai. Newest addition(Maratha Military Landscapes,2025) bhi isi\n state mein hai — trend continue hota hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Maharashtra mein SABSE ZYADA cultural sites hain(6) — Ajanta, Ellora, Elephanta Caves, CST, Victorian Gothic\n Ensemble, aur newest Maratha Military Landscapes(2025).\n\n\n\n4. Natural Sites — Khangchendzonga Ka Ekmatra-Mixed Trap\n ● Kaziranga(1985,Assam) · Manas(1985,Assam) · Keoladeo(1985,Rajasthan) — teeno SAME year\n ● Sundarbans(1987,WB) · Western Ghats(2012 — 5 states: Maharashtra,Goa,Karnataka,TN,Kerala)\n ● Nanda Devi & Valley of Flowers(1988-2005, Uttarakhand) — DO baar listed hua(extension)\n ● Khangchendzonga National Park(2016,Sikkim) — India ka EKMATRA \"MIXED\" category site\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Khangchendzonga = Natural-list mein, par asal mein Mixed\" trick\n Khangchendzonga NATURAL SITES ki list mein dikhta hai(is chapter ke section mein) par ACTUALLY iski official category\n \"MIXED\" hai(natural+cultural dono significance). Yaad rakho: \"Khang-chen = Khaas(special) category — akela site jo\n dono world mein fit baithta hai\" — jab bhi \"India ka mixed WHS kaunsa hai\" poochha jaaye, Khangchendzonga hi sahi\n answer hai, koi doosra nahi.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Khangchendzonga National Park(Sikkim) India ka EKMATRA \"Mixed\" category UNESCO site hai — natural aur cultural\n dono significance combine karta hai, purely natural nahi.\n\n\n\n5. Intangible Heritage — 2008 Ka Triple-Start\n ● PEHLI 3 entries(SAB 2008): Vedic Chanting, Ramlila, Kutiyattam(Sanskrit Theatre)\n ● LATEST(2023): Garba dance\n ● Yoga(2016), Kumbh Mela(2017), Durga Puja(2021) — recent additions\n ● Chhau dance, Mudiyettu, Kalbelia dance — sab 2010 mein\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"2008 = Triple-Launch-Year\" trick\n Intangible Heritage list 2008 mein TEEN entries ke saath shuru hui — Vedic Chanting, Ramlila, Kutiyattam — ek saath\n\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 17 · UNESCO World Heritage Sites in India\n\n launch hue, isliye \"first entry\" poochhe jaane par teeno hi sahi answer honge(single answer nahi). Yaad rakho: \"2008 =\n 3-in-1 shuruaat\" — Garba(2023) is list ka SABSE NAYA/latest hai, dono extremes(shuruaat aur latest) pakka karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Pehle 3 Intangible Heritage entries(sab 2008): Vedic Chanting, Ramlila, Kutiyattam. Latest(2023): Garba dance.\n\n\n\n6. UNESCO Creative Cities — Music-Wali 3 Cities\n ● UCCN shuru: 2009 by UNESCO — 7 creative fields cover karta hai\n ● MUSIC field: Gwalior(2023), Chennai(2017), Varanasi(2015) — TEEN cities share karti hain\n ● FOLK ARTS & CRAFTS: Srinagar(2021) + Jaipur(2015) — DO cities share karti hain\n ● Mumbai(Film,2019) · Hyderabad(Gastronomy,2019) · Kozhikode(Literature,2023)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"3-Music, 2-Folk-Arts\" grouping trick\n UCCN mein DO fields multiple cities share karti hain — MUSIC(3 cities: Gwalior-Chennai-Varanasi) aur FOLK ARTS(2\n cities: Srinagar-Jaipur). Yaad rakho: \"Music=3-gaana(teen shehar gaate hain), Folk-Arts=2-haath(do shehar kaarigari\n karte hain)\" — baaki fields(Film-Mumbai, Gastronomy-Hyderabad, Literature-Kozhikode) EK-EK city ke saath UNIQUE\n hain, mix mat karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Teen Indian cities \"Music\" creative field share karti hain: Gwalior, Chennai, aur Varanasi. Do cities \"Folk Arts and\n Crafts\" share karti hain: Srinagar aur Jaipur.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"44 sites: 35-Cultural(most)-7-Natural-1-Mixed → Agra Fort+Taj Mahal(1983,twins) → Maharashtra(6\n sites,champion) → Khangchendzonga(only Mixed site) → Intangible: 2008-triple-start(Vedic+Ramlila+Kutiyattam)-\n Garba(2023,latest) → UCCN: Music-3cities(Gwalior-Chennai-Varanasi), Folk-Arts-2cities(Srinagar-Jaipur)\"\n\n\n                            Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Agra Fort aur Taj Mahal DONO 1983 mein listed hue — same year, same state(UP), ek ko doosre se pehle mat\n samjho.\n 2) Khangchendzonga National Park(Sikkim) India ka EKMATRA Mixed-category UNESCO site hai, purely natural nahi.\n 3) UCCN mein 3 cities MUSIC share karti hain(Gwalior,Chennai,Varanasi); 2 cities FOLK ARTS share karti\n hain(Srinagar,Jaipur).\n\n\n           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.17 UNESCO World Heritage Sites in India\n\n                                            Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 18 · Art and Culture\n\n                  ART AND CULTURE — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 18 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (state-dance pairing, multi-state overlaps,\ndate-confusion between similar festivals), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Musical Instruments — Bharat Muni Ka 4-Category System\n  ● Tantu Vadya(String): Veena,Sitar,Sarod,Violin,Santoor · Sushir Vadya(Wind): Flute,Shehnai,Conch\n  ● Ghan Vadya(Solid,no-string-no-air): Manjira,Khartal,Bell · Avanaddha Vadya(Percussion): Dhol,Tabla,Pakhawaj\n  ● Shehnai — SAAT(7) holes, auspicious instrument\n  ● Bismillah Khan(Shehnai,Bharat Ratna 2001) — Independence Day par Red Fort mein perform kiya\n  ● Purandara Dasa — Father of Carnatic Music · Pt. Vishwa Mohan Bhatt — Mohan Veena ke inventor\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"T-S-G-A\" 4-category classification trick\n Bharat Muni ne 4 category banayi apne MATERIAL/mechanism ke hisaab se — Tantu(taar/string) → Sushir(hawa/wind)\n → Ghan(thos/solid, na taar na hawa) → Avanaddha(khichi-hui-jhilli/percussion). Yaad rakho: \"T-S-G-A\" — \"Taar-Saans-\n Ghar-Awaaz\" jaisa silly-hook bana lo. Shehnai ke 7 holes ek specific number-fact hai, isse flute se alag rakhna(dono\n wind instruments hain par exact hole-count alag).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Shehnai ke SAAT holes hote hain aur ise ek auspicious instrument maana jaata hai — MCQs mein flute ke saath aksar\n confuse kiya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n2. Classical Dance I — 8-vs-9 Dance-Count Trap\n  ● SNA officially 8 classical dances recognise karta hai — Chhau ko Ministry of Culture ALAG se recognise karta hai,\n  isse 9 ho jaata hai\n  ● 8 dances: Bharatanatyam(TN), Kuchipudi(AP), Kathakali(Kerala), Mohiniyattam(Kerala), Kathak(UP),\n  Manipuri(Manipur), Odissi(Odisha), Sattriya(Assam)\n  ● Bharatanatyam — \"5th Veda\", banned 1910(British), revived by Rukmini Devi Arundale(Kalakshetra,Chennai)\n  ● Kathakali makeup: Pacha(Green=noble), Kathi(evil), Thadi-Red(demons)/White(divine)/Black(hunters),\n  Minukku(gentle-female)\n  ● Kuchipudi — Tarangam(brass-plate balance), founded by Siddhendra Yogi\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"8-Official + 1-Chhau = 9\" count-trick\n SNA(Sangeet Natak Akademi) ki OFFICIAL list mein 8 dances hain — par MINISTRY OF CULTURE Chhau ko SEPARATELY\n recognise karta hai, isliye government-level total 9 ho jaata hai. Yaad rakho: \"8=SNA ka number, 9=Sarkar ka\n number(Chhau add hone ke baad)\" — jab bhi \"total classical dances\" poochha jaaye, exam kaunsi body reference kar\n raha hai wo dekho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 18 · Art and Culture\n\n SNA officially 8 classical dances recognise karta hai; Chhau ko Ministry of Culture separately recognise karta hai, jisse\n govt. total 9 ho jaata hai — yeh distinction aksar test ki jaati hai.\n\n\n\n3. Classical Dance II — Sattriya Ka Sabse-Naya-Recognition\n ● Kathak(UP) — \"Katha\"(story) se naam, modern revival: Leila Sokhey(Menaka), Lucknow/Jaipur/Varanasi\n Gharanas\n ● Manipuri — Vaishnavism(Raasleela) se influenced, Golden Era: Bhagyachandra aur Keerti Chandra\n ● Odissi(Odisha) — Maharis/Devadasis origin, evidence: Udayagiri & Khandagiri caves(2nd century BCE)\n ● Kelucharan Mohapatra — Odissi ka first dancer jisne Padma Vibhushan(2000) jeeta\n ● Sattriya(Assam) — SABSE RECENTLY(2000) classical status mila, popularized by Srimanta Sankardeva(15th\n century)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Sattriya = Sabse Naya Sadasya\" trick\n Sattriya SABSE RECENTLY(2000) classical dance ka status paayi — jabki iski PRACTICE 15th century se(Sankardeva ke\n time se) chal rahi thi. Yaad rakho: \"Sattriya = Purani practice, Naya recognition\" — 500+ saal purana style tha, par\n OFFICIAL classical tag sirf 2000 mein mila. Ye \"9th slot\"(Chhau ke saath) confuse kiya jaata hai — Sattriya asli 8 mein SE\n HAI(recent addition), Chhau ALAG 9th category hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Sattriya sabse recently recognized classical dance hai(2000) — commonly Chhau ke 9th slot ke saath test kiya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n4. Folk & Tribal Dances — Chhau Ka 3-State Overlap\n ● Chhau — BIHAR, JHARKHAND, AUR WEST BENGAL — TEENO states mein appear karta hai\n ● Rajasthan: Ghoomar, Kalbelia(UNESCO 2010), Kathputli\n ● Kerala: Mudiyettu, Chakyar Koothu(UNESCO 2010) · Himachal: Noti(Guinness World Record)\n ● Tribal dances: Mundari(Munda tribe,Jharkhand), Ghumar(Bhil tribe,multi-state), Sarhul(Oraon tribe)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Chhau = Teen-Rajya-ka-Mehman\" trick\n Chhau EK dance form hai jo TEEN alag states(Bihar, Jharkhand, West Bengal) mein practice hoti hai — koi single-state\n ka nahi hai. Yaad rakho: \"Chhau = Poorvi-3-Rajya\"(eastern-3-states) — jab bhi \"Chhau kaunse state ka hai\" poochha\n jaaye, single answer nahi hai, teeno options sahi ho sakte hain. Ye classification-trap chapter 3(classical-vs-tribal split)\n mein bhi repeat hoti hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Chhau Bihar, Jharkhand AUR West Bengal — teeno states mein appear karta hai — ek multi-state overlap jo frequently\n test kiya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 18 · Art and Culture\n5. Folk Songs — State-Song Naam-Signature Match\n ● UP: Kalgiturra, Phaag, Alha Gayan, Birha · Bihar/Jharkhand: Chhath Songs(Bihar's biggest festival se connect)\n ● Maharashtra: Lavani, Powada, Ovi · West Bengal: Baul, Bhatiyali\n ● Assam: Bihu song · Punjab: Tappa · Rajasthan: Halra, Gangaur\n ● Manipur: Baul(bhi hai, West Bengal se ALAG context mein) — naam-overlap dhyan se dekho\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Chhath-Song = Bihar ka Signature\" trick\n Bihar/Jharkhand ke folk songs mein \"Chhath Songs\" naam se ek category HAI — ye DIRECTLY Bihar ke sabse important\n festival(Chhath Puja) se connect karta hai. Yaad rakho: \"Jahan Chhath manaya jaata hai, wahi Chhath Songs bhi gaaye\n jaate hain\" — festival aur folk-song dono ek hi region(Bihar) ko point karte hain, is cross-link se dono yaad rakhna easy\n ho jaata hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Bihar/Jharkhand folk songs mein Chhath Songs shamil hain — directly Bihar ke sabse important festival, Chhath Puja,\n se connect karta hai.\n\n\n\n6. Religious Festivals — Navroz vs Vaisakhi Date-Confuse Trap\n ● Navroz(Parsi New Year) — 21 MARCH · Khordad Sal(Parsi) — Zarathust ka birthday\n ● Vaisakhi(Sikhism) — 1st VAISHAKH(April), Khalsa Panth founding by Guru Gobind Singh\n ● Diwali — Kartik amavasya, Rama's return · Ganesh Chaturthi — Balgangadhar Tilak ne start kiya\n ● Buddha Purnima — birth+enlightenment+Mahaparinirvana TEENO ek hi din(Vaisakha purnima)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Navroz-March, Vaisakhi-April\" month-lock\n Navroz(Parsi) aur Vaisakhi(Sikh) dono \"New Year/harvest-type\" festivals lagte hain isliye confuse hote hain — par\n Navroz MARCH mein hai(21 March, spring-equinox se related), Vaisakhi APRIL mein hai(harvest-season). Yaad rakho:\n \"Navroz=Naya-saal-jaldi(March), Vaisakhi=Vasant-baad(April)\" — dono \"naye-saal-jaisi\" feel dete hain par alag\n calendar-month, alag religion.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Navroz(Parsi New Year, 21 March) ko Vaisakhi(Sikh, April) ke saath confuse mat karo — date-based MCQs mein yeh\n commonly mix up ho jaate hain.\n\n\n\n7. National & Regional Festivals — Chhath Puja Ka Sun-Devta Connect\n ● Republic Day(26 Jan) · Independence Day(15 Aug) · Gandhi Jayanti(2 Oct, International Non-Violence Day)\n ● Chhath — Bihar(sabse famous)+Eastern UP, Sun God aur wife Usha ko dedicated\n ● Onam(Kerala) — Chera king Mahabali se related · Bihu(Assam) — 3 baar saal mein(Rangali,Bhogali,Kangali)\n ● Mahamastakabhisheka(Shravanabelagola,Karnataka) — Bahubali statue, HAR 12 SAAL mein\n ● Nanda Devi Raj Jat(Uttarakhand) — bhi HAR 12 SAAL mein\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 18 · Art and Culture\n\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"12-Saal-Wale Do Festivals\" trick\n Do ALAG festivals HAR 12 SAAL mein hote hain — Mahamastakabhisheka(Karnataka, Bahubali statue anointing) aur\n Nanda Devi Raj Jat(Uttarakhand, pilgrimage). Yaad rakho: \"12-saal-cycle = South(Karnataka) aur North(Uttarakhand)\n dono mein hai\" — same cycle-number, do alag desh ke kone, do alag purpose(ek statue-ritual, ek pilgrimage).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Chhath Puja = Bihar ka sabse important festival, Sun God aur unki wife Usha ko dedicated — BPSC ke liye high-priority.\n\n\n\n8. Fairs & Melas — Kumbh Mela Ke 4 Location-River Match\n ● Kumbh Mela(har 12 saal): Haridwar(GANGA), Prayagraj(SANGAM), Nasik(GODAVARI), Ujjain(KSHIPRA/SHIPRA)\n ● Pushkar Camel Fair(Rajasthan) — world's LARGEST camel fair\n ● Sonpur Cattle Fair(Bihar, Ganga-Gandak sangam) — ASIA's largest cattle fair\n ● Surajkund Fair(Haryana) — International Crafts Mela\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"HA-PRA-NA-UJ = River-Match\" chain\n 4 Kumbh locations, 4 ALAG nadiyan — Haridwar(GANGA) → Prayagraj(SANGAM, teen nadiyon ka milan) →\n Nasik(GODAVARI) → Ujjain(KSHIPRA). Yaad rakho: \"HA-PRA-NA-UJ\" bolke chaaron pehle letters se river-match lock\n karo. Sonpur(Asia's largest CATTLE fair) aur Pushkar(world's largest CAMEL fair) — dono \"largest\" hain par jaanwar\n alag, scope alag(Asia vs World).\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Kumbh Mela ki 4 locations aur rivers options mein frequently mismatch kar di jaati hain — Haridwar(Ganga),\n Prayagraj(Sangam), Nasik(Godavari), Ujjain(Kshipra/Shipra).\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Instruments: T-S-G-A(4-category) → Classical dances: 8(SNA)+1(Chhau)=9 → Sattriya(2000,sabse naya) → Chhau(3-\n state: Bihar-Jharkhand-WB) → Chhath Songs=Bihar signature → Navroz(March)-Vaisakhi(April) → 12-saal-festivals:\n Mahamastakabhisheka-Nanda Devi Raj Jat → Kumbh: HA-PRA-NA-UJ river-match\"\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) SNA officially 8 classical dances recognise karta hai; Chhau ko Ministry of Culture ALAG se recognise karta hai —\n govt total 9 ho jaata hai.\n 2) Chhau Bihar, Jharkhand AUR West Bengal — teeno states mein appear karta hai, single-state ka nahi hai.\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 18 · Art and Culture\n\n3) Kumbh Mela ki 4 locations-rivers: Haridwar(Ganga), Prayagraj(Sangam), Nasik(Godavari), Ujjain(Kshipra) —\nmismatch mat karo.\n\n\n                   Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.18 Art and Culture\n\n\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 5","Static GK · Chapter 19 · Abbreviations\n\n                    ABBREVIATIONS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n                       Static GK · Chapter 19 · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (multi-meaning abbreviations, one-word-\nswap similar-sounding pairs, spelling traps), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. A–C — CAD Ka Triple-Meaning Trap\n  ● CAD = Command Area Development / Computer-Aided Design / Current Account Deficit — 3 ALAG meanings\n  ● ASLV = Augmented Satellite Launch Vehicle · ASI = Archaeological Survey of India\n  ● BHIM = Bharat Interface for Money · BARC = Bhabha Atomic Research Centre\n  ● CAG = Comptroller and Auditor-General · CBDT = Central Board of Direct Taxes · CTBT = Comprehensive Test Ban\n  Treaty\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"CAD Teen Roop\" trick\n CAD teen ALAG fields mein teen ALAG matlab rakhta hai — Command Area Development(irrigation/agriculture),\n Computer-Aided Design(engineering), Current Account Deficit(economics). Yaad rakho: \"CAD ka context dekho\" —\n economics ka question ho toh Current Account Deficit hi sabse zyada aata hai exam mein, par baaki do options bhi\n valid hain agar context alag ho.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n CAD ke context ke hisaab se 3 alag full forms hain(Command Area Development / Computer-Aided Design / Current\n Account Deficit) — options mein aksar economics wala(Current Account Deficit) test kiya jaata hai.\n\n\n\n2. D–G — FERA vs FEMA Ka Repealed-vs-Current Trap\n  ● FERA = Foreign Exchange Regulation Act — REPEALED(purana law)\n  ● FEMA = Foreign Exchange Management Act — CURRENT law, 1999 mein FERA ko REPLACE kiya\n  ● LASER-jaisa naam wala GATE = Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering(engineering test, laser nahi)\n  ● GATT = General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade — WTO ka PREDECESSOR\n  ● GSLV = Geosynchronous Satellite Launch Vehicle · DRDO = Defence Research and Development Organization\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"FERA=Purana, FEMA=Naya\" replace-trick\n FERA aur FEMA dono \"Foreign Exchange\" se shuru hote hain isliye confuse hote hain — par FERA(1973 ka law) 1999\n mein FEMA se REPLACE ho gaya. Yaad rakho: \"FERA=First(purana), FEMA=Modern(naya)\" — dono naam mein alag alag\n last-word bhi hai: Regulation(FERA,rigid-control) vs Management(FEMA,flexible-approach) — naam-badlaav khud\n regulatory-philosophy-shift bhi darshata hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n FERA(repealed) vs FEMA(current law jo ise replace karta hai) — ek classic mix-up. FEMA ne 1999 mein FERA ko replace\n kiya.\n\n\n\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 19 · Abbreviations\n3. H–K — IMF Ka Do-Meaning Trap\n ● IMF = International Monetary Fund(usual/common meaning) / Indian Mountaineering Foundation(rare context)\n ● INTERPOL = International Criminal Police Organization\n ● ICMR = Indian Council of Medical Research · ICAR = Indian Council of Agricultural Research\n ● JAM = Jan Dhan Aadhaar Mobile · KCC = Kisan Call Centre OR Kisan Credit Card(dono valid)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"IMF = Money-Wala-Zyada-Common\" trick\n IMF DEFAULT/common meaning International Monetary Fund hai(finance-related exam ka regular topic), par Indian\n Mountaineering Foundation(mountaineering-context mein) bhi hai. Yaad rakho: \"Question sports/mountaineering ke\n baare mein ho toh IMF=Mountaineering, warna default IMF=Monetary Fund\" — context hi decide karta hai. KCC bhi isi\n tarah do meaning rakhta hai(Call Centre ya Credit Card), dono agriculture-related hain isliye kam confuse hota hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n IMF usually International Monetary Fund hota hai, lekin Indian Mountaineering Foundation bhi ho sakta hai —\n question ka context matter karta hai.\n\n\n\n4. L–N — LASER vs MASER Ka One-Word-Swap Trap\n ● LASER = Light Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation\n ● MASER = Microwave Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation — SIRF pehla word alag\n ● NITI = National Institution for Transforming India · NABARD = National Bank for Agriculture and Rural\n Development\n ● MUDRA = Micro Units Development and Refinance Agency Limited\n ● LOC = Line of Control · LTTE = Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Light vs Microwave = Ekmatra Antar\" trick\n LASER aur MASER ka structure BILKUL SAME hai — sirf PEHLA word badalta hai: LIGHT(LASER) vs\n MICROWAVE(MASER). Baaki poora phrase(\"Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation\") SAME hai dono mein.\n Yaad rakho: \"L for Light, M for Microwave\" — pehla letter hi decide karta hai, baaki sab identical hai, isliye options\n mein ye SABSE ZYADA confuse karne wala swap-trap hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n LASER aur MASER sirf ek word se differ karte hain — Light vs Microwave amplification. Options mein ek common swap\n trick hai.\n\n\n\n5. O–Q — PSLV vs GSLV vs ASLV Ka Orbit-Type Trap\n ● PSLV = Polar Satellite Launch Vehicle — POLAR orbit ke liye\n ● GSLV = Geosynchronous Satellite Launch Vehicle — GEOSYNCHRONOUS orbit ke liye\n ● ASLV = Augmented Satellite Launch Vehicle — EARLY experimental vehicle(chapter A mein bhi)\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 19 · Abbreviations\n ● OPEC = Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries · PAN = Permanent Account Number\n ● PMKVY = Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"P-Polar, G-Geo, A-Augmented\" ISRO-vehicle trick\n Teen ISRO launch vehicles, teen ALAG letters, teen ALAG matlab — PSLV(P=Polar orbit), GSLV(G=Geosynchronous\n orbit), ASLV(A=Augmented, purana/experimental). Yaad rakho: \"Pehla letter hi orbit-type bata deta hai\" — P-S-G-A\n pattern se full-form khud-ba-khud yaad aa jaata hai, sirf first-letter ka matlab pakka karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n PSLV vs GSLV vs ASLV — sab ISRO launch vehicles hain lekin alag orbit types ke liye; PSLV(Polar),\n GSLV(Geosynchronous), ASLV(Augmented, early experimental).\n\n\n\n6. R–S — RDX Ka Do-Accepted-Naam Trap\n ● RDX = Research Department Explosive OR Royal Demolition Explosive — DONO accepted, alag sources mein\n ● RADAR = Radio Detection and Ranging · RAW = Research and Analysis Wing\n ● SEBI = Securities and Exchange Board of India · SWIFT = Society for Worldwide Interbank Financial\n Telecommunication\n ● STD = Subscribers Trunk Dialing · SIDBI = Small Industries Development Bank of India\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"RDX = Do Naam, Ek Cheez\" trick\n RDX ek explosive hai jiske DO different full-forms accepted hain — Research Department Explosive(British origin naam)\n aur Royal Demolition Explosive(alternate naam). Yaad rakho: \"RDX = R-D-X, dono R-wale naam(Research/Royal) chalte\n hain\" — exam mein agar dono options mein se koi bhi RDX ke saath match kare, dono SAHI ho sakte hain, single\n \"correct\" answer expect mat karo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n RDX ke do accepted full forms hain — Research Department Explosive aur Royal Demolition Explosive — dono alag\n sources mein appear karte hain.\n\n\n\n7. T–Z — UNO Ka Singular-Nations Spelling-Trap\n ● UNO = United Nations Organization — \"NATIONS\" hamesha PLURAL hai(\"Nation\" singular GALAT hai)\n ● UNESCO = United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization\n ● UNICEF = United Nations International Children's Emergency Fund\n ● TRIPS = Trade-Related Aspects of Intellectual Property Rights\n ● VSSC = Vikram Sarabhai Space Centre · WWF = World Wide Fund for Nature\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Nations = Plural Hamesha\" spelling-lock\n UNO ka correct full-form \"United NATIONS Organization\" hai — kamzor sources mein galti se \"United Nation\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 19 · Abbreviations\n\n Organizations\"(singular Nation, plural Organizations) likha jaata hai, jo GALAT hai. Yaad rakho: \"UN khud hi Multiple\n Nations ka group hai, isliye Nations hamesha PLURAL\" — country-count zyada hai, isliye plural sahi hai, singular nahi.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n UNO ka full form United Nations Organization hai — commonly weak sources mein galat \"United Nation\n Organizations\" likha jaata hai; hamesha sahi singular \"Nations\" use karo(Nations hi plural sahi hai, Organization\n singular sahi hai).\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"CAD: 3-meanings(irrigation/design/economics) → FERA(purana)-FEMA(naya,1999) → IMF: Monetary(common)-\n Mountaineering(rare) → LASER(Light)-MASER(Microwave) → ISRO: PSLV(Polar)-GSLV(Geo)-ASLV(Augmented) → RDX:\n Research-Department OR Royal-Demolition(dono sahi) → UNO: Nations(plural-hamesha)\"\n\n\n                           Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) CAD ke 3 alag full forms hain — Command Area Development, Computer-Aided Design, Current Account Deficit —\n context dekho.\n 2) LASER(Light) aur MASER(Microwave) sirf pehla word alag hai, baaki phrase SAME hai — is one-word-swap trap ko\n pakka karo.\n 3) UNO = United NATIONS Organization — \"Nations\" hamesha plural, \"Nation Organizations\" galat spelling hai.\n\n\n                      Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.19 Abbreviations\n\n\n\n\n                                           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4","Static GK · Chapter 20 · Important Days\n\n                  IMPORTANT DAYS — MEMORY TRICK SHEET\n               Static GK · Chapter 20 (Final Chapter) · Sirf Yaad Rakhne Wali Cheezein — Tricks + Chains\n\nYe sheet full notes nahi hai — sirf wahi cheezein hain jo bhoolne wali hoti hain (same-date multiple observances, similar-\nnaam days at different dates), har ek ke saath ek trick jisse woh chipak jaaye dimaag mein.\n\n1. Jan–Feb — Martyrs' Day Ka Do-Date Trap\n  ● 30 Jan: Martyrs' Day(Gandhi assassination) · 23 Mar(agle mahine): Martyrs' Day(Bhagat Singh,Rajguru,Sukhdev)\n  ● 9 Jan: Pravasi Bharatiya Divas · 12 Jan: National Youth Day(Vivekananda) · 23 Jan: Parakram Diwas(Bose)\n  ● 26 Jan: Republic Day/International Customs Day · 25 Jan: Tourism Day/National Voters' Day(SAME date)\n  ● 28 Feb: National Science Day · 4 Feb: World Cancer Day\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Do Martyrs' Day, Do Alag Shaheed\" trick\n \"Martyrs' Day\" naam DO ALAG dates pe hai — 30 January(Gandhi ki hatya) aur 23 March(Bhagat Singh-Rajguru-\n Sukhdev ki phaansi). Yaad rakho: \"30-Gandhi(January mein akela), 23-Trio(March mein teen shaheed)\" — number bhi\n hint deta hai: 30(Gandhi,SINGLE martyr) vs 23(trio ki date, teeno ek saath). Exam \"Martyrs' Day\" poochhe toh\n CONTEXT dekho(kis vyakti ka zikr hai) tabhi sahi date pakdo.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n Do \"Martyrs' Day\" dates exist hain — 30 January(Gandhi ki assassination) aur 23 March(Bhagat Singh, Rajguru,\n Sukhdev). In dono ko confuse mat karo.\n\n\n\n2. Mar–Apr — Amjad Ali Khan Day Ka Cross-Topic Link\n  ● 23 March: Martyrs' Day(Bhagat Singh) / World Meteorological Day — SAME date, DO observance\n  ● 8 March: International Women's Day · 22 March: World Water Day\n  ● 14 April: B.R. Ambedkar Jayanti · 22 April: World Earth Day\n  ● 20 April: \"Amjad Ali Khan Day\" — US state Massachusetts ne declare kiya, sarod-maestro ke liye\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Amjad Ali Khan = Art-Culture aur Important-Days ka Cross-link\" trick\n Amjad Ali Khan(sarod player, jo Chapter 18-Art&Culture mein bhi hai) ke liye US ke Massachusetts state ne 20 April ko\n unka SPECIAL DAY declare kiya — ye ek UNIQUE fact hai jo do chapters(Art-Culture + Important Days) ko cross-link\n karta hai. Yaad rakho: \"Sarod-wale Amjad Ali Khan ko VIDESH(Massachusetts) mein bhi din mila\" — India ke bahar kisi\n Indian musician ke liye declared day, isliye special/unusual fact hai.\n\n\n\n3. May–Jun — International Yoga Day Aur Environment Day\n  ● 21 June: International Yoga Day · 5 June: World Environment Day\n  ● 1 May: International Labour Day · 12 May: International Nurses Day(Florence Nightingale)\n  ● 22 May: International Day for Biological Diversity · 31 May: World No Tobacco Day\n  ● 23 June: International Olympic Day · 29 June: National Statistics Day\n                                          Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 1","Static GK · Chapter 20 · Important Days\n\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"5-June-Paryavaran, 21-June-Yoga\" same-month trick\n June mahine mein DO high-profile international days hain — 5 June(Environment) aur 21 June(Yoga), 16 din ka gap.\n Yaad rakho: \"5=Prithvi(Environment, EARLY month), 21=Sharir(Yoga, SUMMER SOLSTICE, longest-day-of-year)\" — 21\n June khud summer solstice hai, isliye Yoga Day ki date astronomically bhi significant hai, sirf random date nahi.\n\n\n\n4. Jul–Aug — National Javelin Day Ka Neeraj-Chopra-Connect\n ● 7 August: National Handloom Day / National Javelin Day(since 2021, Neeraj Chopra ke Olympic gold ke baad)\n ● 29 August: National Sports Day(Major Dhyan Chand's Birthday) — ALAG date, ALAG occasion\n ● 14 August: Partition Horrors Remembrance Day(since 2021) / Pakistan Independence Day — SAME date\n ● 26 July: Kargil Vijay Diwas · 6 August: Hiroshima Day\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"Javelin-7, Sports-29\" August-split trick\n August mein DO sports-related days hain jo confuse hote hain — National JAVELIN Day(7 August, SPECIFIC sport,\n Chopra ke gold ke baad naya introduce hua) vs National SPORTS Day(29 August, OVERALL sports, Dhyan Chand ki\n birthday, purana/traditional). Yaad rakho: \"7=Naya-Specific(Javelin,recent), 29=Purana-General(Sports,traditional)\" —\n chota number(7)=naya/specific, bada number(29)=purana/general.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n National Javelin Day(7 August, since 2021) Neeraj Chopra ke Olympic gold ke baad introduce kiya gaya tha — National\n Sports Day(29 August) ke saath confuse karna aasaan hai.\n\n\n\n5. Sep–Oct — 2 October Ka Triple-Observance\n ● 2 October = TEEN observance ek saath: Gandhi Jayanti + Lal Bahadur Shastri Jayanti + International Day of Non-\n Violence\n ● 5 September: National Teachers' Day(Radhakrishnan) · 15 September: National Engineers' Day\n ● 1 October: International Day of Older Persons / World Vegetarian Day — bhi DOUBLE\n ● 20 October: World Statistics Day(HAR 5 SAAL mein) — regular annual nahi\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"2 October = Triple-Combo Date\" trick\n 2 October SABSE ZYADA-LOADED date hai chapter mein — TEEN alag observance: Gandhi Jayanti(bada leader), Shastri\n Jayanti(dusra PM, SAME birthday), International Day of Non-Violence(UN ne Gandhi ke sammaan mein banaya). Yaad\n rakho: \"2 October = Do-PM-ka-Janamdin(Gandhi+Shastri) + UN-ka-Tribute\" — teeno ek hi date pe, exam kisi bhi ek ko\n poochh sakta hai.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n 2 October ek double/triple observance hai — Gandhi Jayanti, Lal Bahadur Shastri Jayanti, aur International Day of Non-\n Violence, sab same date par.\n\n\n                                        Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 2","Static GK · Chapter 20 · Important Days\n6. Nov–Dec — Consumer Rights Day Ka World-vs-National Trap\n ● National Consumer Rights Day: 24 DECEMBER · World Consumer Rights Day: 15 MARCH(chapter 3 mein) —\n DONO ALAG\n ● 26 November: National Law Day / Constitution Day / Guru Nanak Dev Jayanti — TEEN observance\n ● 14 November: National Children's Day / World Diabetes Day · 15 November: Tribal Pride Day(Birsa Munda)\n ● 25 December: National Good Governance Day(Vajpayee's birthday)\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"World-March, National-December\" Consumer-Rights split\n Consumer Rights Day DO ALAG level par exist karta hai — WORLD(15 March, global observance) aur NATIONAL(24\n December, India-specific). Yaad rakho: \"World=Vasant(March,spring), National=Varsh-ant(December,year-end)\" —\n dono \"Consumer Rights\" naam share karte hain par TEEN mahine ka gap nahi, POORE 9 mahine ka gap hai(March se\n December) — inhe merge mat karo, dono real/separate observance hain.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n National Consumer Rights Day(24 Dec) World Consumer Rights Day(15 March) se alag hai — dono exist karte hain,\n inhe merge mat karo.\n\n\n\n7. UN Decades & Years — 2025 Ka Dual-Theme\n ● 2025 = DUAL theme: International Year of Glaciers' Preservation AND Quantum Science and Technology\n ● 2023: Millets · 2024: Camelids · 2026: Women Farmers · 2027: Sustainable/Resilient Tourism\n ● 2019-2028: Nelson Mandela Decade of Peace · 2021-2032: Decade of Indigenous Languages\n ● 2016-2025: Decade of Action on Nutrition\n\n\n 💡 TRICK — \"2025 = Do-Theme-Ek-Saal\" trick\n 2025 EKMATRA saal hai(is list mein) jiske DO theme hain ek saath — Glaciers' Preservation AUR Quantum Science and\n Technology, dono SAME year(2025) ke liye declare hue. Yaad rakho: \"2025 = Double-Duty saal\" — baaki saare\n International Years(2023-Millets, 2024-Camelids, 2026-Women Farmers) ka EK-EK theme hai, sirf 2025 hi exception hai\n do themes ke saath.\n\n\n\n ⚠ EXAM TRAP\n 2025 ka dual theme hai — Glaciers' Preservation AND Quantum Science and Technology — dono same year ke liye\n declare kiye gaye hain.\n\n\n\n🔗 Master Memory Chain — Poora Chapter Ek Saath\n 🔗 1-Line Revision Chain (bolke revise karo)\n \"Martyrs' Day: 30-Jan(Gandhi)-23-Mar(trio) → Amjad Ali Khan Day(20 April, Massachusetts) → Environment(5 June)-\n Yoga(21 June, solstice) → Javelin(7 Aug,naya)-Sports(29 Aug,purana) → 2 October=triple(Gandhi+Shastri+Non-\n Violence) → Consumer Rights: World(15 March)-National(24 Dec) → 2025=dual-theme(Glaciers+Quantum)\"\n\n                                       Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 3","Static GK · Chapter 20 · Important Days\n\n\n                          Roz sone se pehle ye ek line bol lo — jitni baar bologe utna pakka hoga.\n\n⚠ Top 3 Traps Jo Sabse Zyada Aate Hain\n 1) Do \"Martyrs' Day\" dates hain — 30 January(Gandhi) aur 23 March(Bhagat Singh-Rajguru-Sukhdev) — merge mat\n karo.\n 2) National Javelin Day(7 Aug, Chopra ke baad naya) aur National Sports Day(29 Aug, Dhyan Chand, purana) — alag\n dates, alag purpose.\n 3) World Consumer Rights Day(15 March) aur National Consumer Rights Day(24 December) — dono real hain, alag\n scope.\n\n\n           Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Static GK Memory Tricks · Ch.20 Important Days (FINAL CHAPTER)\n\n\n\n\n                                         Exam Fusion Prep | examfusionprep.com · Page 4"];
